PathwayData.put("data/reading_writing/units/L05U2.json",{"strand":"reading_writing","level":5,"cefr":"B1a","unit":2,"theme":"Healthy Mind, Healthy Body","essential_question":"What habits help us stay healthy and balanced?","schema_version":"1.0","core_words":["balanced diet","nutrient","energy","fitness","routine","stress","relax","habit","hydrate","vitamin","injury","recover","wellbeing","posture"],"recycled_words":["water","sleep","exercise","healthy","energy","because","so","opinion","reason","fact","hook","dehydration","hydrate"],"rubrics":[{"id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","title":"Analytic writing rubric","traits":[{"name":"Ideas","name_ar":"الأفكار","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear, interesting and fully developed with strong details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة وممتعة ومدعومة بتفاصيل قوية."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear and have enough details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة ومعها تفاصيل كافية."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"My main idea is there but needs more details.","descriptor_ar":"فكرتي الرئيسية موجودة لكنها تحتاج إلى تفاصيل أكثر."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"My ideas are unclear or very few.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري غير واضحة أو قليلة جدًا."}]},{"name":"Organization","name_ar":"التنظيم","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Clear beginning, middle and end; ideas flow with linking words.","descriptor_ar":"بداية ووسط ونهاية واضحة، والأفكار مترابطة بكلمات الربط."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Clear order with some linking words.","descriptor_ar":"ترتيب واضح مع بعض كلمات الربط."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Some order, but parts are mixed up.","descriptor_ar":"يوجد بعض الترتيب لكن بعض الأجزاء غير مرتبة."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Ideas are not in order.","descriptor_ar":"الأفكار غير مرتبة."}]},{"name":"Vocabulary","name_ar":"المفردات","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"I use exact, varied words, including new unit words, correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات دقيقة ومتنوعة، منها كلمات الوحدة الجديدة، بشكل صحيح."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"I use some new words correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم بعض الكلمات الجديدة بشكل صحيح."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"I use simple words; some are repeated or wrong.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات بسيطة، وبعضها مكرر أو غير صحيح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"I use very few words; the meaning is hard to understand.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات قليلة جدًا ويصعب فهم المعنى."}]},{"name":"Sentence fluency","name_ar":"سلاسة الجمل","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My sentences are complete, varied in length and easy to read aloud.","descriptor_ar":"جملي كاملة ومتنوعة الطول وسهلة القراءة بصوت عالٍ."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Most sentences are complete, with some variety.","descriptor_ar":"معظم جملي كاملة مع بعض التنويع."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Many sentences are short or start the same way.","descriptor_ar":"كثير من جملي قصيرة أو تبدأ بالطريقة نفسها."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Sentences are incomplete or run together.","descriptor_ar":"جملي ناقصة أو متداخلة."}]},{"name":"Conventions","name_ar":"قواعد الكتابة","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Capitals, punctuation, spelling and grammar are almost always correct.","descriptor_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة وعلامات الترقيم والإملاء والقواعد صحيحة دائمًا تقريبًا."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"A few mistakes that do not affect meaning.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء قليلة لا تؤثر في المعنى."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Several mistakes; the meaning is sometimes unclear.","descriptor_ar":"عدة أخطاء، والمعنى أحيانًا غير واضح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Many mistakes make it hard to read.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء كثيرة تجعل القراءة صعبة."}]}]}],"lessons":[{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS1","title":"Word Power: Healthy Mind, Healthy Body","lesson_type":"vocabulary","objectives":["read, say and use 14 words about health and wellbeing and 4 Tier 2 words (maintain, benefit, recommend, essential)","build nouns with the suffixes -ness (adjective → noun) and -ment (verb → noun)","spell suffix words correctly (happy → happiness; move → movement)"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة ونطق واستخدام 14 كلمة عن الصحة والعافية و4 كلمات أكاديمية.","بناء الأسماء باللاحقتين -ness (صفة ← اسم) و-ment (فعل ← اسم).","تهجئة الكلمات ذات اللواحق بشكل صحيح."],"success_criteria":["I can use the health words correctly in sentences.","I can tell if a word is made from an adjective (-ness) or a verb (-ment).","I can use the new nouns in my own sentences with correct spelling."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع استخدام كلمات الصحة في جمل بشكل صحيح.","أستطيع معرفة هل الكلمة مشتقة من صفة (-ness) أو فعل (-ment).","أستطيع استخدام الأسماء الجديدة في جملي بتهجئة صحيحة."],"map_area":"Vocabulary: Acquisition and Use","vocabulary":[{"word":"balanced diet","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbælənst ˈdaɪət/","definition":"eating the right amounts of different kinds of food","arabic":"نظام غذائي متوازن","example":"A balanced diet includes fruit, vegetables, grains and protein.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"nutrient","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈnutriənt/","definition":"a substance in food that your body needs to grow and stay healthy","arabic":"عنصر غذائي","example":"Milk has nutrients like calcium.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"energy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛnərdʒi/","definition":"the power your body needs to move, think and grow","arabic":"طاقة","example":"Breakfast gives you energy for the morning.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"fitness","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɪtnəs/","definition":"being strong and healthy because you exercise","arabic":"لياقة بدنية","example":"Swimming improves your fitness.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"routine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ruˈtin/","definition":"the things you do regularly in the same order","arabic":"روتين","example":"My morning routine starts with prayer and breakfast.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"stress","pos":"noun","ipa":"/strɛs/","definition":"a feeling of worry because of problems or too much work","arabic":"توتر / ضغط","example":"Exams can cause stress.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"relax","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈlæks/","definition":"to rest and become calm","arabic":"يسترخي","example":"I relax by reading a book.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V07","tier":"core"},{"word":"habit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhæbɪt/","definition":"something you do often, almost without thinking","arabic":"عادة","example":"Washing your hands is a good habit.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V08","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V08","tier":"core"},{"word":"hydrate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈhaɪˌdreɪt/","definition":"to drink enough water so your body has what it needs","arabic":"يروي الجسم بالماء","example":"Hydrate before and after sport.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V09","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V09","tier":"core"},{"word":"vitamin","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈvaɪtəmɪn/","definition":"a natural substance in food that keeps your body healthy","arabic":"فيتامين","example":"Oranges have vitamin C.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V10","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V10","tier":"core"},{"word":"injury","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɪndʒəri/","definition":"harm to the body, for example a cut or a broken bone","arabic":"إصابة","example":"Warm up to avoid an injury.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V11","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V11","tier":"core"},{"word":"recover","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈkʌvər/","definition":"to become healthy again after an illness or injury","arabic":"يتعافى","example":"He recovered quickly from the flu.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V12","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V12","tier":"core"},{"word":"wellbeing","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈwɛlˌbiɪŋ/","definition":"feeling healthy, happy and comfortable in body and mind","arabic":"العافية / جودة الحياة","example":"Sleep is important for your wellbeing.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V13","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V13","tier":"core"},{"word":"posture","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɑstʃər/","definition":"the way you hold your body when you sit or stand","arabic":"وضعية الجسم","example":"Sit up straight – good posture protects your back.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V14","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V14","tier":"core"},{"word":"maintain","pos":"verb","ipa":"/meɪnˈteɪn/","definition":"to keep something at the same good level","arabic":"يحافظ على","example":"Exercise helps you maintain a healthy weight.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V15","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V15","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"benefit","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/ˈbɛnəfɪt/","definition":"a good result or advantage; to be helped by something","arabic":"فائدة / يستفيد","example":"One benefit of walking is better sleep.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V16","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V16","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"recommend","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌrɛkəˈmɛnd/","definition":"to say that something is good or the best thing to do","arabic":"يوصي","example":"Doctors recommend eight to ten hours of sleep for teenagers.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V17","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V17","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"essential","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪˈsɛnʃəl/","definition":"very important and necessary","arabic":"أساسي / ضروري","example":"Water is essential for life.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V18","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V18","tier":"tier2"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **suffix** is a small part added to the **end** of a word. It changes the word's **job** (part of speech). The suffixes **-ness** and **-ment** both make **nouns** (names of things or ideas).\n\n**-ness** is added to **adjectives**: *fit → fitness, kind → kindness, tired → tiredness, weak → weakness, aware → awareness*. If the adjective ends in a consonant + **y**, change **y → i**: *happy → happiness, lazy → laziness, healthy → healthiness*.\n\n**-ment** is added to **verbs**: *move → movement, improve → improvement, treat → treatment, enjoy → enjoyment, develop → development, equip → equipment*. Usually you **keep the e**: *move → movement, achieve → achievement*. To check: take off the suffix – is the base an **adjective** or a **verb**?","examples":["*Swimming is good for your **fitness**.* (fit = adjective → fitness = noun)","*Too much screen time can cause **tiredness** and headaches.* (tired → tiredness)","*Sharing your lunch is an act of **kindness**.* (kind → kindness)","*Laughing with friends brings **happiness**.* (happy → happ**i**ness: y → i)","*Daily **movement** keeps your joints healthy.* (move → movement: keep the e)","*I saw a big **improvement** in my running time.* (improve → improvement)","*The doctor gave him **treatment** for his injury.* (treat → treatment)","*The gym has new **equipment**.* (equip → equipment)","Sort it: **adjective + ness** (fitness, sadness) / **verb + ment** (movement, enjoyment)."],"common_errors":["✗ happyness → ✓ happiness (Change **y → i** before -ness.)","✗ movment → ✓ movement (Keep the **e** before -ment.)","✗ fitment → ✓ fitness (fit is an adjective → **-ness**.)","✗ Swimming is good for your fit. → ✓ Swimming is good for your fitness. (After **your**, use the noun.)","✗ Exercise is benefit for health. → ✓ Exercise is beneficial for health. / Exercise benefits your health. (benefit is a noun or a verb.)","✗ Doctors recommend to sleep 9 hours. → ✓ Doctors recommend sleeping 9 hours. (recommend + **-ing**.)","✗ Water is essential to drink it. → ✓ Water is essential for life. (essential **for** + noun.)"],"arabic":"اللاحقة جزء يضاف إلى آخر الكلمة فيغيّر نوعها. واللاحقتان -ness و-ment تكوّنان أسماء.\n\n-ness تضاف إلى الصفات: fit ← fitness، kind ← kindness. وإذا انتهت الصفة بحرف ساكن + y نحوّل y إلى i: happy ← happiness.\n\n-ment تضاف إلى الأفعال: move ← movement، improve ← improvement، وغالبًا نبقي حرف e.\n\nللتحقق: احذف اللاحقة؛ هل الأصل صفة أم فعل؟ وانتبه: recommend + -ing، وessential for."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"Stretch up high! Today we talk about a healthy mind and a healthy body.","on_screen":"Healthy Mind, Healthy Body 💪🧠","visual":"Omar and Layla stretch in the schoolyard at sunrise."},{"time":"00:25–01:20","narration":"A balanced diet gives you nutrients, vitamins and energy. Hydrate! Keep your fitness and good posture!","on_screen":"balanced diet · nutrient · vitamin · energy · hydrate · fitness · posture","visual":"A plate of food groups, a water bottle, a child sitting straight."},{"time":"01:20–01:55","narration":"Good habits and a daily routine reduce stress. Relax, recover from injuries and protect your wellbeing!","on_screen":"habit · routine · stress · relax · injury · recover · wellbeing","visual":"A calm reading corner; a bandaged ankle healing."},{"time":"01:55–03:00","narration":"Suffix power! Add -ness to adjectives: fit → fitness. Add -ment to verbs: move → movement!","on_screen":"-ness = adjective + ness · -ment = verb + ment","visual":"Word blocks snap together: happy + ness → happiness (y → i)."},{"time":"03:00–03:30","narration":"Doctors recommend healthy habits – they're essential, and the benefits help you maintain your wellbeing!","on_screen":"maintain · benefit · recommend · essential","visual":"A doctor gives a thumbs-up."}],"captions_ar":["تمدّد للأعلى! اليوم نتحدث عن عقل سليم وجسم سليم.","النظام الغذائي المتوازن يمنحك العناصر الغذائية والفيتامينات والطاقة. اشرب الماء وحافظ على لياقتك ووضعيتك!","العادات الجيدة والروتين اليومي يقللان التوتر. استرخِ وتعافَ واحمِ عافيتك!","قوة اللواحق! أضف -ness إلى الصفات و-ment إلى الأفعال!","الأطباء يوصون بالعادات الصحية؛ فهي أساسية وفوائدها تحافظ على عافيتك!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, upbeat female fitness coach, speed 0.95."},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","instructions_ar":"اختر الكلمة الصحيحة.","items":[{"q":"Eating the right amounts of different foods is a ___.","answer":"balanced diet","explanation":"Balanced diet.","explanation_ar":"نظام غذائي متوازن.","options":["posture","routine","injury","balanced diet"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Oranges and lemons are full of ___ C.","answer":"vitamin","explanation":"Vitamin.","explanation_ar":"فيتامين.","options":["stress","posture","vitamin","fitness"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Sit up straight at your desk – good ___ protects your back.","answer":"posture","explanation":"Posture.","explanation_ar":"وضعية الجسم.","options":["posture","energy","habit","nutrient"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Faris broke his arm. The ___ happened during a football match.","answer":"injury","explanation":"Injury.","explanation_ar":"الإصابة.","options":["injury","routine","vitamin","benefit"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Before a long run in the heat, you must ___ by drinking water.","answer":"hydrate","explanation":"Hydrate.","explanation_ar":"تروي جسمك.","options":["recover","hydrate","relax","maintain"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"My morning ___ is the same every day: pray, wash, eat breakfast and walk to school.","answer":"routine","explanation":"Routine.","explanation_ar":"روتين.","options":["injury","routine","nutrient","posture"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS1-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Suffixes -ness and -ment. Choose.","instructions_ar":"اللاحقتان -ness و-ment: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which word is made from an ADJECTIVE + -ness?","answer":"fitness","explanation":"fit = adjective.","explanation_ar":"fitness.","options":["movement","treatment","equipment","fitness"],"dok":1,"skill":"suffixes","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which word is made from a VERB + -ment?","answer":"improvement","explanation":"improve = verb.","explanation_ar":"improvement.","options":["kindness","sadness","improvement","weakness"],"dok":1,"skill":"suffixes","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which spelling of the noun from *happy* is correct?","answer":"happiness","explanation":"y → i.","explanation_ar":"happiness.","options":["happiness","happyness","happness","happiment"],"dok":2,"skill":"spelling","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which spelling of the noun from *move* is correct?","answer":"movement","explanation":"Keep the e.","explanation_ar":"movement.","options":["movment","moveness","moving-ment","movement"],"dok":2,"skill":"spelling","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*After a week of rest, there was a big **improvement** in his injury.* What does *improvement* mean?","answer":"the act of getting better","explanation":"improve + ment.","explanation_ar":"تحسّن.","options":["the act of getting worse","the act of getting better","a kind of medicine","a doctor"],"dok":2,"skill":"suffixes","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Staying up late can cause **tiredness** the next day.* What is the base word and its part of speech?","answer":"tired – adjective","explanation":"Take off -ness.","explanation_ar":"tired صفة.","options":["tire – noun","tiring – verb","tired – adjective","tiredly – adverb"],"dok":3,"skill":"suffixes","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS1-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word bank.","instructions_ar":"استخدم بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"Doctors ________ that children sleep nine to twelve hours a night.","answer":"recommend","explanation":"Advise.","explanation_ar":"يوصون.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Water is ________ for life; we cannot live without it.","answer":"essential","explanation":"Necessary.","explanation_ar":"أساسي.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"One ________ of walking to school is that you start the day with energy.","answer":"benefit","explanation":"Advantage.","explanation_ar":"فائدة.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Regular exercise helps you ________ a healthy weight.","answer":"maintain","explanation":"Keep.","explanation_ar":"تحافظ على.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Our school bought new sports ________ for the gym.","answer":"equipment","explanation":"equip + ment.","explanation_ar":"معدات.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"A smile and a kind word are small acts of ________.","answer":"kindness","explanation":"kind + ness.","explanation_ar":"لطف.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS1-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write with the new words.","instructions_ar":"اكتب باستخدام الكلمات الجديدة.","items":[{"q":"Write two sentences: one with a -ness word and one with a -ment word.","answer":"Swimming improves my fitness. I enjoy the movement of the water around me.","explanation":"-ness + -ment.","explanation_ar":"-ness + -ment.","dok":2,"skill":"suffixes","stage":"production"},{"q":"Describe your evening routine. Use *relax* and *routine*.","answer":"My evening routine is simple: I finish my homework, relax with a book and go to bed at nine.","explanation":"Two words.","explanation_ar":"كلمتان.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"},{"q":"What is one benefit of a balanced diet?","answer":"A balanced diet gives your body the nutrients and energy it needs to grow and learn.","explanation":"Benefit.","explanation_ar":"فائدة.","dok":2,"skill":"explain","stage":"production"},{"q":"Which healthy habit do you find the hardest? How could you improve it?","answer":"Drinking enough water. I could carry a water bottle and drink a glass with every meal.","explanation":"Reflect.","explanation_ar":"تأمّل.","dok":3,"skill":"reflect","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Suffix Fitness Circuit","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Fitness circuit: a base word jogs onto the screen; the child chooses -ness or -ment and types the correct spelling. Correct words fill an energy bar; spelling the y → i words correctly gives a bonus.","Teams rotate through five stations (2 minutes each).","At each station, they build as many real nouns as possible with -ness or -ment.","They write each word correctly and its part of speech.","At the end, teams use three of their words in sentences.","Each correct word = 1 point; each correct sentence = 2 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which word means *a substance in food that your body needs*?","answer":"nutrient","explanation":"Nutrient.","explanation_ar":"عنصر غذائي.","options":["nutrient","posture","routine","injury"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"What does the suffix *-ness* usually make?","answer":"a noun from an adjective","explanation":"Rule.","explanation_ar":"اسمًا من صفة.","options":["a verb from a noun","a noun from an adjective","an adjective from a verb","a plural"],"dok":1,"skill":"suffixes"},{"q":"*He rested for two weeks and **recovered** from his injury.* *Recovered* means ___.","answer":"became healthy again","explanation":"Recover.","explanation_ar":"تعافى.","options":["got hurt again","started a sport","went to school","became healthy again"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which feeling word is built from a verb + *-ment*?","answer":"enjoyment","explanation":"enjoy = verb.","explanation_ar":"enjoyment.","options":["enjoyment","sadness","fitness","darkness"],"dok":1,"skill":"suffixes"},{"q":"Which sentence about sleep advice is correct?","answer":"Doctors recommend sleeping nine hours a night.","explanation":"recommend + -ing.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Doctors recommend to sleep nine hours a night.","Doctors recommend sleeping nine hours a night.","Doctors recommends sleeping nine hours a night.","Doctors recommend sleep nine hours a night."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which spelling is correct?","answer":"laziness","explanation":"y → i.","explanation_ar":"laziness.","options":["lazyness","laziness","lazness","lazement"],"dok":2,"skill":"spelling"},{"q":"*Water is **essential** for our bodies.* *Essential* means ___.","answer":"very important and necessary","explanation":"Essential.","explanation_ar":"ضروري.","options":["not needed","dangerous","very important and necessary","expensive"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which noun completes the sentence: *Yoga can reduce stress and bring a feeling of ___.*","answer":"calmness","explanation":"calm (adj) + ness.","explanation_ar":"calmness.","options":["calmment","calmly","calmness","calming"],"dok":2,"skill":"suffixes"},{"q":"Which word does NOT belong in the group *treatment, movement, improvement, weakness*?","answer":"weakness","explanation":"weak = adjective (-ness).","explanation_ar":"weakness.","options":["treatment","movement","improvement","weakness"],"dok":3,"skill":"suffixes"},{"q":"Sara drinks water only once a day and feels tired at school. Which habit would help her MOST?","answer":"carrying a water bottle and drinking regularly through the day","explanation":"Apply.","explanation_ar":"حمل قارورة ماء.","options":["drinking a large soda at lunch","sleeping in class","carrying a water bottle and drinking regularly through the day","skipping breakfast"],"dok":3,"skill":"apply"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'balanced diet': a plate divided into food groups"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'nutrient': food icons with arrows to a body"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'energy': a child running with a battery icon full"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'fitness': a child jogging in a park"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'routine': a daily schedule with clock icons"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'stress': a student holding his head over books"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'relax': a child reading calmly on a cushion"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V08","prompt":"Picture for the word 'habit': a child washing hands"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V09","prompt":"Picture for the word 'hydrate': a child drinking from a water bottle"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V10","prompt":"Picture for the word 'vitamin': an orange with a letter C"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V11","prompt":"Picture for the word 'injury': a bandaged ankle"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V12","prompt":"Picture for the word 'recover': a child smiling after being sick"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V13","prompt":"Picture for the word 'wellbeing': a happy child with a heart and brain icon"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V14","prompt":"Picture for the word 'posture': a child sitting straight at a desk"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V15","prompt":"Picture for the word 'maintain': a balance scale level"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V16","prompt":"Picture for the word 'benefit': a plus sign with a smiling face"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V17","prompt":"Picture for the word 'recommend': a doctor giving advice"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V18","prompt":"Picture for the word 'essential': a glass of water with a star"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-01","prompt":"Students practicing healthy habits at school."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-02","prompt":"Pictures of health words."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS1-03","prompt":"Suffix machines for -ness and -ment."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V01","script":"balanced diet. A balanced diet includes fruit, vegetables, grains and protein."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V02","script":"nutrient. Milk has nutrients like calcium."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V03","script":"energy. Breakfast gives you energy for the morning."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V04","script":"fitness. Swimming improves your fitness."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V05","script":"routine. My morning routine starts with prayer and breakfast."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V06","script":"stress. Exams can cause stress."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V07","script":"relax. I relax by reading a book."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V08","script":"habit. Washing your hands is a good habit."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V09","script":"hydrate. Hydrate before and after sport."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V10","script":"vitamin. Oranges have vitamin C."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V11","script":"injury. Warm up to avoid an injury."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V12","script":"recover. He recovered quickly from the flu."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V13","script":"wellbeing. Sleep is important for your wellbeing."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V14","script":"posture. Sit up straight – good posture protects your back."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V15","script":"maintain. Exercise helps you maintain a healthy weight."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V16","script":"benefit. One benefit of walking is better sleep."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V17","script":"recommend. Doctors recommend eight to ten hours of sleep for teenagers."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-V18","script":"essential. Water is essential for life."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Stretch up high! Today we talk about a healthy mind and a healthy body. A balanced diet gives you nutrients, vitamins and energy. Hydrate! Keep your fitness and good posture! Good habits and a daily routine reduce stress. Relax, recover from injuries and protect your wellbeing! Suffix power! Add -ness to adjectives: fit → fitness. Add -ment to verbs: move → movement! Doctors recommend healthy habits – they're essential, and the benefits help you maintain your wellbeing!"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS2","title":"The Science of Sleep","lesson_type":"close_reading","objectives":["read a science article of about 370 words about sleep","follow a scientific explanation: stages in order and what happens in each stage","explain causes and effects in a science text with evidence"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة مقال علمي من نحو 420 كلمة عن النوم.","تتبّع الشرح العلمي: المراحل بالترتيب وما يحدث في كل مرحلة.","شرح الأسباب والنتائج في نص علمي بالدليل."],"success_criteria":["I can name the stages of a sleep cycle in order.","I can say what happens in each stage.","I can explain a cause and effect from the text (screens → less melatonin → hard to fall asleep)."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع تسمية مراحل دورة النوم بالترتيب.","أستطيع قول ما يحدث في كل مرحلة.","أستطيع شرح سبب ونتيجة من النص."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"cycle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsaɪkəl/","definition":"a set of stages that happen again and again in the same order","arabic":"دورة","example":"A sleep cycle lasts about 90 minutes.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"stage","pos":"noun","ipa":"/steɪdʒ/","definition":"one part of a process","arabic":"مرحلة","example":"Deep sleep is an important stage.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"heartbeat","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɑrtˌbit/","definition":"the regular movement of your heart","arabic":"نبضات القلب","example":"Your heartbeat slows down in sleep.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"hormone","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhɔrˌmoʊn/","definition":"a natural chemical in the body that controls how it grows and works","arabic":"هرمون","example":"The body releases a growth hormone in deep sleep.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"concentrate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈkɑnsənˌtreɪt/","definition":"to give all your attention to something","arabic":"يركّز","example":"It is hard to concentrate when you are tired.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"germ","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dʒɝm/","definition":"a very small living thing that can make you sick","arabic":"جرثومة","example":"Sleep helps your body fight germs.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"grumpy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɡrʌmpi/","definition":"in a bad mood and easily annoyed","arabic":"متجهّم / سيّئ المزاج","example":"I feel grumpy when I don't sleep enough.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"Science texts often explain **how something works**. They describe a **process** in **stages** and tell **what happens** in each stage and **why**.\n\nTo follow the explanation: (1) use the **headings** to find each part; (2) look for **stage words** in **bold** (light sleep, deep sleep, REM sleep); (3) note **what happens** in each stage; (4) find **cause–effect signal words**: *because, so, as a result, if … then*.\n\nThen **explain it in your own words**. A good explanation tells the stages **in order** and the **effects**: *During deep sleep, the body repairs muscles, so we wake up stronger.*","examples":["**Stage 1 – light sleep:** *your muscles relax and your heartbeat slows down.*","**Stage 2 – deep sleep:** *your body repairs muscles and … releases a hormone that helps you grow.*","**Stage 3 – REM sleep:** *your eyes move quickly … most dreams happen … helps you store memories.*","**Cycle:** *After REM sleep, a new cycle begins* – four to six cycles a night.","**Cause → effect:** *If you don't sleep enough → it becomes harder to concentrate.*","**Cause → effect:** *sleep helps the body fight germs* → too little sleep → *easier to get sick* (*because*).","**Chain:** blue light from screens → *your body makes less melatonin* → *As a result, it takes longer to fall asleep.*","**Own words:** *Screens before bed trick your brain into thinking it is daytime, so you feel less sleepy.*","**Numbers as evidence:** *children aged 6 to 12 … 9 to 12 hours a night.*"],"common_errors":["✗ Mixing up the order of the stages. → ✓ Light sleep → deep sleep → REM sleep, then a new cycle. (Follow the text order.)","✗ Sleep is when the brain switches off. → ✓ The brain is very active, especially in REM sleep. (Check the facts!)","✗ Giving a stage name without what happens. → ✓ Add what happens: In deep sleep, the body repairs muscles. (Stage + effect.)","✗ Children needs 9 hours. → ✓ Children need 9 to 12 hours. (Plural → **need**.)","✗ Screens makes you sleepy. → ✓ Screens make it harder to feel sleepy. (Check meaning and agreement.)","✗ Because I was tired. → ✓ I couldn't concentrate because I was tired. (A **because** clause needs a main clause.)"],"arabic":"تشرح النصوص العلمية كيف يعمل الشيء؛ فتصف العملية في مراحل وتذكر ما يحدث في كل مرحلة ولماذا.\n\nلتتبّع الشرح: استخدم العناوين، وابحث عن أسماء المراحل بالخط العريض، ودوّن ما يحدث فيها، وابحث عن كلمات السبب والنتيجة.\n\nثم اشرحه بكلماتك بالترتيب مع النتائج، مثل: في النوم العميق يصلح الجسم العضلات فنستيقظ أقوى.\n\nمعلومة صحيحة: الدماغ نشيط جدًا أثناء النوم، خاصة في مرحلة حركة العين السريعة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"You spend about one third of your life asleep. But is your brain really switched off?","on_screen":"The Science of Sleep 😴🧠","visual":"A clock spins through the night; a sleeping child glows with brain activity."},{"time":"00:25–02:00","narration":"Why do we spend about one third of our lives asleep?…","on_screen":"(article, section by section)","visual":"A sleep-cycle diagram: light sleep, deep sleep (muscles repair), REM (eyes moving, dream bubbles); a phone's blue light; a tired child in class."},{"time":"02:00–02:40","narration":"Follow the stages: light sleep → deep sleep → REM sleep → a new cycle!","on_screen":"Stage → what happens","visual":"A circle of three colored arrows repeats four to six times across a night timeline."},{"time":"02:40–03:15","narration":"Cause and effect: blue light → less melatonin → harder to fall asleep.","on_screen":"Cause → Effect chain","visual":"Three linked boxes light up one after another."},{"time":"03:15–03:30","narration":"Same bedtime, no screens, a dark room – sweet dreams!","on_screen":"Tips for better sleep 🌙","visual":"A child puts a phone in a drawer and turns off the light."}],"captions_ar":["تقضي نحو ثلث حياتك نائمًا. لكن هل يتوقف دماغك حقًا؟","لماذا نقضي نحو ثلث حياتنا نائمين؟…","تتبّع المراحل: نوم خفيف ← نوم عميق ← نوم حركة العين السريعة ← دورة جديدة!","سبب ونتيجة: الضوء الأزرق ← ميلاتونين أقل ← صعوبة في النوم.","موعد نوم ثابت، بلا شاشات، وغرفة مظلمة… أحلامًا سعيدة!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, calm female science presenter, speed 0.95."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Science of Sleep","body":"Why do we spend about one third of our lives asleep? For a long time, people thought sleep was just \"switching off.\" Today, scientists know that while you sleep, your brain and body are very busy.\n\n**A Night of Cycles**\n\nSleep is not one long, even rest. Every night, you go through several sleep cycles. Each cycle lasts about 90 minutes and has different stages.\n\nIn **light sleep**, your muscles relax and your heartbeat slows down. It is easy to wake up. In **deep sleep**, your breathing becomes slow and even, and it is hard to wake you. This is when your body repairs muscles and, in young people, releases a hormone that helps you grow. In **REM sleep** (rapid eye movement), your eyes move quickly behind your eyelids, and most dreams happen. Your brain is very active. Scientists believe this stage helps you store memories and learn new skills.\n\nAfter REM sleep, a new cycle begins. Most people go through four to six cycles every night.\n\n**What Happens Without Enough Sleep?**\n\nIf you don't sleep enough, you may feel tired and grumpy the next day. It becomes harder to concentrate in class, remember new words and solve problems. Over time, too little sleep can also make it easier to get sick, because sleep helps the body fight germs.\n\n**How Much Sleep Do You Need?**\n\nSleep experts recommend that children aged 6 to 12 sleep 9 to 12 hours a night. Teenagers need 8 to 10 hours. However, many students get much less, often because of late-night screens.\n\n**Screens and Sleep**\n\nPhones, tablets and computers give off blue light. This light can tell your brain that it is still daytime, so your body makes less melatonin, the natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy. As a result, it takes longer to fall asleep.\n\n**Tips for Better Sleep**\n\n**1.** Go to bed and wake up at the same time every day, even at weekends. **2.** Turn off screens at least one hour before bed. **3.** Keep your bedroom dark, quiet and cool. **4.** Avoid tea, coffee and energy drinks in the evening.\n\nSleep is not wasted time. It is when your body and brain get ready for tomorrow.","word_count":367,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L05-U2-LS2-1","genre":"informational","role":"main","difficulty":"550L–750L","glossary":[{"word":"cycle","definition":"a set of stages that happen again and again in the same order","arabic":"دورة"},{"word":"hormone","definition":"a natural chemical in the body that controls how it grows and works","arabic":"هرمون"},{"word":"melatonin","definition":"a natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy when it gets dark","arabic":"الميلاتونين"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the article. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ المقال واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"About how much of our lives do we spend asleep?","answer":"about one third","explanation":"Introduction.","explanation_ar":"نحو الثلث.","options":["about one half","about one third","about one tenth","almost all"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How long does one sleep cycle last?","answer":"about 90 minutes","explanation":"A Night of Cycles.","explanation_ar":"نحو 90 دقيقة.","options":["about 10 minutes","about 5 hours","about 90 minutes","a whole night"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"In which stage do most dreams happen?","answer":"REM sleep","explanation":"REM.","explanation_ar":"مرحلة حركة العين السريعة.","options":["REM sleep","light sleep","deep sleep","when you are awake"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does the body do during deep sleep?","answer":"repairs muscles and releases a growth hormone","explanation":"Deep sleep.","explanation_ar":"يصلح العضلات ويفرز هرمون النمو.","options":["moves the eyes quickly","makes blue light","wakes up easily","repairs muscles and releases a growth hormone"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How many hours of sleep do experts recommend for children aged 6 to 12?","answer":"9 to 12 hours","explanation":"How Much.","explanation_ar":"9–12 ساعة.","options":["5 to 6 hours","8 hours exactly","13 to 15 hours","9 to 12 hours"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What is melatonin?","answer":"a natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy","explanation":"Glossary / Screens.","explanation_ar":"مادة تُشعرك بالنعاس.","options":["a natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy","a kind of screen","a vitamin in oranges","a stage of sleep"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS2-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Stages, causes and effects. Choose.","instructions_ar":"المراحل والأسباب والنتائج: اختر.","items":[{"q":"What is the correct order of the stages in one sleep cycle?","answer":"light sleep → deep sleep → REM sleep","explanation":"Process.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["REM sleep → light sleep → deep sleep","light sleep → deep sleep → REM sleep","deep sleep → REM sleep → light sleep","REM sleep → deep sleep → light sleep"],"dok":1,"skill":"sequence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why can screens make it harder to fall asleep?","answer":"Blue light makes the body produce less melatonin.","explanation":"Cause → effect.","explanation_ar":"الضوء الأزرق يقلل الميلاتونين.","options":["Screens are too heavy.","Blue light makes the body produce less melatonin.","Screens make the room cold.","Screens give you vitamins."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"guided"},{"q":"According to the article, what is one effect of not sleeping enough?","answer":"It becomes harder to concentrate and remember.","explanation":"Effect.","explanation_ar":"صعوبة التركيز والتذكر.","options":["It becomes harder to concentrate and remember.","You grow taller faster.","You dream more in class.","Your eyes move quickly all day."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why can too little sleep make it easier to get sick?","answer":"Sleep helps the body fight germs.","explanation":"because.","explanation_ar":"لأن النوم يساعد على مقاومة الجراثيم.","options":["Germs like the dark.","Beds are full of germs.","Sleep gives you blue light.","Sleep helps the body fight germs."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which signal phrase introduces an effect in *As a result, it takes longer to fall asleep*?","answer":"As a result","explanation":"Signal words.","explanation_ar":"As a result.","options":["it takes","longer","As a result","to fall"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why does the writer say people once thought sleep was *switching off*?","answer":"to show that scientists now know the brain and body are busy during sleep","explanation":"Author's craft.","explanation_ar":"ليُظهر أن العلم صحّح فكرة قديمة.","options":["to prove that sleep is a waste of time","to explain how to turn off a phone","to show that scientists now know the brain and body are busy during sleep","to describe a machine"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS2-A3","type":"highlight","stage":"freer","instructions":"Find the evidence: Find the evidence.","instructions_ar":"ابحث عن الدليل.","items":[{"q":"Underline the sentence that explains how REM sleep may help learning.","answer":"Scientists believe this stage helps you store memories and learn new skills.","explanation":"Evidence.","explanation_ar":"الدليل.","evidence":"Scientists believe this stage helps you store memories and learn new skills.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L05-U2-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["Why do we spend about one third of our lives asleep?","For a long time, people thought sleep was just \"switching off.\"","Today, scientists know that while you sleep, your brain and body are very busy.","**A Night of Cycles**","Sleep is not one long, even rest.","Every night, you go through several sleep cycles.","Each cycle lasts about 90 minutes and has different stages.","In **light sleep**, your muscles relax and your heartbeat slows down.","It is easy to wake up.","In **deep sleep**, your breathing becomes slow and even, and it is hard to wake you.","This is when your body repairs muscles and, in young people, releases a hormone that helps you grow.","In **REM sleep** (rapid eye movement), your eyes move quickly behind your eyelids, and most dreams happen.","Your brain is very active.","Scientists believe this stage helps you store memories and learn new skills.","After REM sleep, a new cycle begins.","Most people go through four to six cycles every night.","**What Happens Without Enough Sleep?**","If you don't sleep enough, you may feel tired and grumpy the next day.","It becomes harder to concentrate in class, remember new words and solve problems.","Over time, too little sleep can also make it easier to get sick, because sleep helps the body fight germs.","**How Much Sleep Do You Need?**","Sleep experts recommend that children aged 6 to 12 sleep 9 to 12 hours a night.","Teenagers need 8 to 10 hours.","However, many students get much less, often because of late-night screens.","**Screens and Sleep**","Phones, tablets and computers give off blue light.","This light can tell your brain that it is still daytime, so your body makes less melatonin, the natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy.","As a result, it takes longer to fall asleep.","**Tips for Better Sleep**","**1.** Go to bed and wake up at the same time every day, even at weekends. **2.** Turn off screens at least one hour before bed. **3.** Keep your bedroom dark, quiet and cool. **4.** Avoid tea, coffee and energy drinks in the evening.","Sleep is not wasted time.","It is when your body and brain get ready for tomorrow."]},{"q":"Underline the sentence that explains what blue light does to the brain.","answer":"This light can tell your brain that it is still daytime, so your body makes less melatonin, the natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy.","explanation":"Cause.","explanation_ar":"السبب.","evidence":"This light can tell your brain that it is still daytime, so your body makes less melatonin, the natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L05-U2-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["Why do we spend about one third of our lives asleep?","For a long time, people thought sleep was just \"switching off.\"","Today, scientists know that while you sleep, your brain and body are very busy.","**A Night of Cycles**","Sleep is not one long, even rest.","Every night, you go through several sleep cycles.","Each cycle lasts about 90 minutes and has different stages.","In **light sleep**, your muscles relax and your heartbeat slows down.","It is easy to wake up.","In **deep sleep**, your breathing becomes slow and even, and it is hard to wake you.","This is when your body repairs muscles and, in young people, releases a hormone that helps you grow.","In **REM sleep** (rapid eye movement), your eyes move quickly behind your eyelids, and most dreams happen.","Your brain is very active.","Scientists believe this stage helps you store memories and learn new skills.","After REM sleep, a new cycle begins.","Most people go through four to six cycles every night.","**What Happens Without Enough Sleep?**","If you don't sleep enough, you may feel tired and grumpy the next day.","It becomes harder to concentrate in class, remember new words and solve problems.","Over time, too little sleep can also make it easier to get sick, because sleep helps the body fight germs.","**How Much Sleep Do You Need?**","Sleep experts recommend that children aged 6 to 12 sleep 9 to 12 hours a night.","Teenagers need 8 to 10 hours.","However, many students get much less, often because of late-night screens.","**Screens and Sleep**","Phones, tablets and computers give off blue light.","This light can tell your brain that it is still daytime, so your body makes less melatonin, the natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy.","As a result, it takes longer to fall asleep.","**Tips for Better Sleep**","**1.** Go to bed and wake up at the same time every day, even at weekends. **2.** Turn off screens at least one hour before bed. **3.** Keep your bedroom dark, quiet and cool. **4.** Avoid tea, coffee and energy drinks in the evening.","Sleep is not wasted time.","It is when your body and brain get ready for tomorrow."]},{"q":"Which tip is connected to the section *Screens and Sleep*?","answer":"Turn off screens at least one hour before bed.","explanation":"Connect sections.","explanation_ar":"إطفاء الشاشات قبل النوم.","options":["Turn off screens at least one hour before bed.","Keep your bedroom cool.","Wake up at the same time every day.","Avoid tea in the evening."],"dok":2,"skill":"text structure","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Why does the article end with *Sleep is not wasted time*?","answer":"to sum up the main idea that sleep is important for body and brain","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"ليختم بالفكرة الرئيسية.","options":["to start a new topic","to give a number","to tell a story","to sum up the main idea that sleep is important for body and brain"],"dok":3,"skill":"conclusions","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS2-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Explain in your own words.","instructions_ar":"اشرح بكلماتك.","items":[{"q":"Explain what happens in each stage of a sleep cycle.","answer":"In light sleep, the muscles relax and the heart slows. In deep sleep, the body repairs itself and grows. In REM sleep, the eyes move quickly, we dream, and the brain stores memories.","explanation":"Three stages.","explanation_ar":"ثلاث مراحل.","dok":2,"skill":"explaining a process","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a cause → effect chain about screens and sleep.","answer":"Screens give off blue light → the body makes less melatonin → it takes longer to fall asleep → we feel tired the next day.","explanation":"Chain.","explanation_ar":"سلسلة.","dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Which sleep tip would be easiest for you, and which would be hardest? Why?","answer":"Keeping my room dark is easy. Turning off screens an hour before bed is hard because I like to watch videos.","explanation":"Reflect.","explanation_ar":"تأمّل.","dok":3,"skill":"reflect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Explain to a younger child why sleep is important (2–3 sentences).","answer":"When you sleep, your body fixes itself and helps you grow. Your brain also saves what you learned today. That's why you need lots of sleep!","explanation":"Explain simply.","explanation_ar":"اشرح ببساطة.","dok":3,"skill":"explaining","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS2-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"The Science of Sleep\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “The Science of Sleep”.","answer":"367 words","title":"The Science of Sleep","body":"Why do we spend about one third of our lives asleep? For a long time, people thought sleep was just \"switching off.\" Today, scientists know that while you sleep, your brain and body are very busy.\n\n**A Night of Cycles**\n\nSleep is not one long, even rest. Every night, you go through several sleep cycles. Each cycle lasts about 90 minutes and has different stages.\n\nIn **light sleep**, your muscles relax and your heartbeat slows down. It is easy to wake up. In **deep sleep**, your breathing becomes slow and even, and it is hard to wake you. This is when your body repairs muscles and, in young people, releases a hormone that helps you grow. In **REM sleep** (rapid eye movement), your eyes move quickly behind your eyelids, and most dreams happen. Your brain is very active. Scientists believe this stage helps you store memories and learn new skills.\n\nAfter REM sleep, a new cycle begins. Most people go through four to six cycles every night.\n\n**What Happens Without Enough Sleep?**\n\nIf you don't sleep enough, you may feel tired and grumpy the next day. It becomes harder to concentrate in class, remember new words and solve problems. Over time, too little sleep can also make it easier to get sick, because sleep helps the body fight germs.\n\n**How Much Sleep Do You Need?**\n\nSleep experts recommend that children aged 6 to 12 sleep 9 to 12 hours a night. Teenagers need 8 to 10 hours. However, many students get much less, often because of late-night screens.\n\n**Screens and Sleep**\n\nPhones, tablets and computers give off blue light. This light can tell your brain that it is still daytime, so your body makes less melatonin, the natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy. As a result, it takes longer to fall asleep.\n\n**Tips for Better Sleep**\n\n**1.** Go to bed and wake up at the same time every day, even at weekends. **2.** Turn off screens at least one hour before bed. **3.** Keep your bedroom dark, quiet and cool. **4.** Avoid tea, coffee and energy drinks in the evening.\n\nSleep is not wasted time. It is when your body and brain get ready for tomorrow.","words":367,"limit":235}],"time_limit_sec":235}],"game":{"name":"Sleep Cycle Race","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Night journey: a sleeping avatar moves through the night; the child drags stage cards into order and matches what happens in each. Correct cycles fill the 'energy bar' for the next morning.","Teams get mixed stage and 'what happens' cards.","They build one full cycle in order and match each stage to its effects.","They repeat the cycle four times on the night timeline.","Bonus: build the screen → melatonin → sleep chain.","Correct cycle = 3 points; each correct match = 1 point; correct chain = 3 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is the main idea of *The Science of Sleep*?","answer":"Sleep is a busy, important time when the body and brain get ready for the next day.","explanation":"Main idea.","explanation_ar":"النوم وقت نشط ومهم.","options":["Screens are always bad.","Dreams are not real.","Sleep is wasted time.","Sleep is a busy, important time when the body and brain get ready for the next day."],"dok":1,"skill":"main idea"},{"q":"*It is hard to **concentrate** when you are tired.* *Concentrate* means ___.","answer":"give all your attention","explanation":"Concentrate.","explanation_ar":"يركّز.","options":["give all your attention","fall asleep","run fast","eat a lot"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"What does REM stand for?","answer":"rapid eye movement","explanation":"Text.","explanation_ar":"حركة العين السريعة.","options":["really easy morning","rest every minute","rapid energy meal","rapid eye movement"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details"},{"q":"How many sleep cycles do most people go through in a night?","answer":"four to six","explanation":"Text.","explanation_ar":"4–6 دورات.","options":["one","ten to twelve","four to six","twenty"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details"},{"q":"Which sentence about teenagers' sleep is correct?","answer":"Teenagers need 8 to 10 hours of sleep.","explanation":"Plural → need.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Teenagers need 8 to 10 hours of sleep.","Teenagers needs 8 to 10 hours of sleep.","Teenagers need sleeping 8 to 10 hours.","Teenagers needing 8 to 10 hours of sleep."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which is a CAUSE in the article?","answer":"blue light from screens","explanation":"Cause vs. effect.","explanation_ar":"سبب.","options":["taking longer to fall asleep","blue light from screens","feeling grumpy","getting sick"],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect"},{"q":"Why does the article use bold words like **deep sleep**?","answer":"to show the important stage names","explanation":"Text features.","explanation_ar":"لإبراز أسماء المراحل.","options":["to make the text longer","to show the important stage names","to show dialogue","to show the title"],"dok":2,"skill":"text features"},{"q":"Faris plays games on his tablet until 11 p.m. and feels tired at school. Which tip would help him MOST?","answer":"Turn off screens at least one hour before bed.","explanation":"Apply.","explanation_ar":"إطفاء الشاشات قبل النوم.","options":["Drink coffee in the evening.","Sleep with the lights on.","Turn off screens at least one hour before bed.","Change his bedtime every night."],"dok":2,"skill":"apply"},{"q":"What can you infer from *Many students get much less, often because of late-night screens*?","answer":"Screen habits are a common reason students don't sleep enough.","explanation":"Inference.","explanation_ar":"عادات الشاشات سبب شائع لقلة النوم.","options":["Students don't need sleep.","Screens help students sleep.","Screen habits are a common reason students don't sleep enough.","Teachers give too much homework."],"dok":3,"skill":"inference"},{"q":"Why does the article tell the stages IN ORDER?","answer":"because sleep is a process that happens in a sequence","explanation":"Text structure.","explanation_ar":"لأن النوم عملية متسلسلة.","options":["because sleep is a process that happens in a sequence","to make it rhyme","because the stages are not important","to tell a story with characters"],"dok":3,"skill":"text structure"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'cycle': a circle of arrows with moon icons"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'stage': steps numbered 1, 2, 3"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'heartbeat': a heart with a pulse line"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'hormone': a simple body diagram with a glowing dot"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'concentrate': a student focusing on a book"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'germ': cartoon germs under a magnifying glass"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'grumpy': a child with a grumpy face"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-01","prompt":"A diagram of the sleep cycle."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-02","prompt":"Blue light from a phone keeping a child awake."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS2-03","prompt":"Four tips for better sleep."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V01","script":"cycle. A sleep cycle lasts about 90 minutes."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V02","script":"stage. Deep sleep is an important stage."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V03","script":"heartbeat. Your heartbeat slows down in sleep."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V04","script":"hormone. The body releases a growth hormone in deep sleep."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V05","script":"concentrate. It is hard to concentrate when you are tired."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V06","script":"germ. Sleep helps your body fight germs."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-V07","script":"grumpy. I feel grumpy when I don't sleep enough."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-T1","script":"Why do we spend about one third of our lives asleep? For a long time, people thought sleep was just \"switching off.\" Today, scientists know that while you sleep, your brain and body are very busy. **A Night of Cycles** Sleep is not one long, even rest. Every night, you go through several sleep cycles. Each cycle lasts about 90 minutes and has different stages. In **light sleep**, your muscles relax and your heartbeat slows down. It is easy to wake up. In **deep sleep**, your breathing becomes slow and even, and it is hard to wake you. This is when your body repairs muscles and, in young people, releases a hormone that helps you grow. In **REM sleep** (rapid eye movement), your eyes move quickly behind your eyelids, and most dreams happen. Your brain is very active. Scientists believe this stage helps you store memories and learn new skills. After REM sleep, a new cycle begins. Most people go through four to six cycles every night. **What Happens Without Enough Sleep?** If you don't sleep enough, you may feel tired and grumpy the next day. It becomes harder to concentrate in class, remember new words and solve problems. Over time, too little sleep can also make it easier to get sick, because sleep helps the body fight germs. **How Much Sleep Do You Need?** Sleep experts recommend that children aged 6 to 12 sleep 9 to 12 hours a night. Teenagers need 8 to 10 hours. However, many students get much less, often because of late-night screens. **Screens and Sleep** Phones, tablets and computers give off blue light. This light can tell your brain that it is still daytime, so your body makes less melatonin, the natural chemical that makes you feel sleepy. As a result, it takes longer to fall asleep. **Tips for Better Sleep** **1.** Go to bed and wake up at the same time every day, even at weekends. **2.** Turn off screens at least one hour before bed. **3.** Keep your bedroom dark, quiet and cool. **4.** Avoid tea, coffee and energy drinks in the evening. Sleep is not wasted time. It is when your body and brain get ready for tomorrow."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS2-VID","script":"You spend about one third of your life asleep. But is your brain really switched off? Why do we spend about one third of our lives asleep?… Follow the stages: light sleep → deep sleep → REM sleep → a new cycle! Cause and effect: blue light → less melatonin → harder to fall asleep. Same bedtime, no screens, a dark room – sweet dreams!"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS3","title":"Author's purpose and point of view: \"Every School Needs a Daily Exercise Break\"","lesson_type":"strategy_paired_text","objectives":["identify the author's purpose: to inform, to explain or to persuade","describe the author's point of view and the words that show it","compare a science article and an opinion text on healthy habits"],"objectives_ar":["تحديد هدف الكاتب: الإعلام أو الشرح أو الإقناع.","وصف وجهة نظر الكاتب والكلمات التي تُظهرها.","مقارنة مقال علمي ونص رأي عن العادات الصحية."],"success_criteria":["I can say why an author wrote a text and give evidence.","I can find opinion words (I believe, should, strongly) and fact words (scientists know, research).","I can explain how the two authors' points of view are alike and different."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع قول سبب كتابة الكاتب للنص مع الدليل.","أستطيع إيجاد كلمات الرأي وكلمات الحقيقة.","أستطيع شرح أوجه التشابه والاختلاف بين وجهتي نظر الكاتبين."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Language, Craft, and Structure","vocabulary":[{"word":"purpose","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɝpəs/","definition":"the reason why something is done or written","arabic":"هدف / غرض","example":"The author's purpose is to persuade.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"persuade","pos":"verb","ipa":"/pərˈsweɪd/","definition":"to make someone agree with you or do something","arabic":"يُقنع","example":"Omar wants to persuade the principal.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"point of view","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pɔɪnt əv vju/","definition":"what an author thinks or feels about a topic","arabic":"وجهة النظر","example":"The author's point of view is clear in the first paragraph.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"oxygen","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɑksɪdʒən/","definition":"the gas in the air that we need to breathe","arabic":"الأكسجين","example":"Exercise sends more oxygen to the brain.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"physical activity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɪzɪkəl ækˈtɪvəti/","definition":"moving your body, for example walking, running or playing","arabic":"النشاط البدني","example":"Children need physical activity every day.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"valuable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈvæljəbəl/","definition":"very useful or important","arabic":"قيّم / ثمين","example":"Lesson time is valuable.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"neutral","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈnutrəl/","definition":"not taking a side; giving facts without opinions","arabic":"محايد","example":"The science article has a neutral tone.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"Every author has a **purpose** – a reason for writing. The main purposes are **to inform** (give facts), **to explain** (tell how or why something works), **to persuade** (make readers agree or act) and **to entertain** (tell a story).\n\nThe author's **point of view** is what he or she **thinks or feels** about the topic. In persuasive texts, it is easy to see: *I believe…, should, must, strongly, Let's…*. In science texts, the point of view is usually **neutral**: the author uses facts and phrases like *scientists know, experts recommend, research shows*.\n\nTo decide: ask **Why did the author write this? What does the author want me to know, think or do?** Then find **evidence**: opinion words, facts, the title, the ending and how the author speaks to the reader.","examples":["*The Science of Sleep* – purpose: **to inform and explain** how sleep works.","Evidence: *Each cycle lasts about 90 minutes and has different stages.* (facts, neutral)","Evidence: *Scientists believe this stage helps you store memories.* (experts, not the author's own feelings)","*Every School Needs a Daily Exercise Break* – purpose: **to persuade** schools to add an exercise break.","Point of view words: ***I believe*** *every school* ***should*** *give students…* / *I* ***strongly*** *believe…*","A persuasive author still uses **facts** as support: *The World Health Organization recommends … 60 minutes.*","Talking to the reader: ***Imagine*** *sitting still…* / ***Let's*** *get moving!* – a call to action.","Counterargument: *Some people say … However, …* – the author answers the other side.","Both authors **agree** that healthy habits help learning, but one **explains** and the other **persuades**."],"common_errors":["✗ The article is persuasive because it gives tips. → ✓ Its main purpose is to explain; the tips support that. (Look at the whole text.)","✗ Omar's text is only facts. → ✓ It uses facts to support an opinion. (Facts can support a persuasive purpose.)","✗ Mixing up the author's view and other people's view. → ✓ 'Some people say…' is the other side, not Omar's view. (Who is speaking?)","✗ The author purpose is persuade. → ✓ The author's purpose is to persuade. (Possessive **'s** + **to** + verb.)","✗ Omar believe schools should… → ✓ Omar believes schools should… (He → **believes**.)","✗ Schools should to give a break. → ✓ Schools should give a break. (**should** + verb (no to).)"],"arabic":"لكل كاتب هدف: الإعلام (حقائق)، أو الشرح (كيف ولماذا)، أو الإقناع (أن نوافق أو نتصرف)، أو الإمتاع (قصة).\n\nوجهة نظر الكاتب هي ما يفكر فيه أو يشعر به تجاه الموضوع. في النص الإقناعي تظهر بكلمات مثل I believe, should, strongly. وفي النص العلمي تكون غالبًا محايدة.\n\nاسأل: لماذا كتب الكاتب هذا؟ ماذا يريدني أن أعرف أو أفكر أو أفعل؟ ثم ابحث عن الدليل.\n\nالنص الإقناعي يستخدم الحقائق أيضًا لدعم الرأي، ويرد على الرأي الآخر (Some people say… However…)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"Why did the author write this? To inform, explain, persuade or entertain?","on_screen":"Author's Purpose & Point of View 🎯","visual":"Four arrows hit a target labelled Inform, Explain, Persuade, Entertain."},{"time":"00:25–01:35","narration":"Imagine sitting still at your desk for six hours…","on_screen":"(Omar's opinion text)","visual":"Students stretching in class; a brain lighting up with oxygen; a clock showing 10 minutes."},{"time":"01:35–02:20","narration":"Opinion words show the author's point of view: I believe, should, strongly, Let's!","on_screen":"Opinion words 💬","visual":"Opinion words glow in Omar's text."},{"time":"02:20–03:00","narration":"The sleep article is neutral: facts, experts and research. Its purpose: to inform and explain.","on_screen":"Neutral vs. persuasive ⚖️","visual":"A balance scale (article) next to a megaphone (opinion)."},{"time":"03:00–03:30","narration":"Both authors agree: healthy habits help you learn!","on_screen":"Same topic, different purposes","visual":"The two texts side by side with a shared heart icon."}],"captions_ar":["لماذا كتب الكاتب هذا؟ للإعلام أم للشرح أم للإقناع أم للإمتاع؟","تخيّل أنك تجلس دون حركة على مقعدك ست ساعات…","كلمات الرأي تُظهر وجهة نظر الكاتب: أعتقد، يجب، بشدة، هيا بنا!","مقال النوم محايد: حقائق وخبراء وأبحاث، وهدفه الإعلام والشرح.","الكاتبان يتفقان: العادات الصحية تساعدك على التعلّم!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, energetic male presenter, speed 0.95. Omar reads his opinion text with passion."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Every School Needs a Daily Exercise Break (by Omar)","body":"Imagine sitting still at your desk for six hours. By the last lesson, your back hurts, your eyes feel heavy and the teacher's words float past you. I believe every school should give students a ten-minute exercise break every day.\n\nFirst, exercise helps us learn. When we move, more blood and oxygen flow to the brain. Many teachers notice that students concentrate better after a short activity break. For example, after our PE lessons, our class always answers more questions in math.\n\nSecond, an exercise break is good for our health. The World Health Organization recommends that children and teenagers do an average of at least 60 minutes of physical activity every day. A daily break would give us part of that time at school.\n\nThird, moving together reduces stress. After a difficult test, a few minutes of stretching or jumping can help us relax and feel happier. It also gives friends a chance to laugh together.\n\nSome people say that exercise breaks waste valuable lesson time. However, a ten-minute break is short, and focused students may learn more in the rest of the lesson than tired students learn in a full one.\n\nFor these reasons, I strongly believe that every school needs a daily exercise break. Let's get moving – our bodies and our brains will thank us!","word_count":218,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L05-U2-LS3-1","genre":"opinion/argument","role":"paired","difficulty":"550L–750L","glossary":[{"word":"oxygen","definition":"the gas in the air that we need to breathe","arabic":"الأكسجين"},{"word":"physical activity","definition":"moving your body, for example walking, running or playing","arabic":"النشاط البدني"},{"word":"valuable","definition":"very useful or important","arabic":"ثمين / قيّم"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Omar's text. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ نص عمر واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What does Omar believe every school should have?","answer":"a ten-minute exercise break every day","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"استراحة رياضية يومية.","options":["longer lessons","a ten-minute exercise break every day","more homework","a new gym only for teams"],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion","text_id":"TXT-RW-L05-U2-LS3-1","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What is Omar's FIRST reason?","answer":"Exercise helps us learn.","explanation":"First, …","explanation_ar":"الرياضة تساعدنا على التعلم.","options":["Exercise reduces stress.","Exercise is fun.","The WHO recommends it.","Exercise helps us learn."],"dok":1,"skill":"reasons","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How much physical activity does the WHO recommend for children and teenagers?","answer":"an average of at least 60 minutes a day","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"60 دقيقة يوميًا على الأقل.","options":["10 minutes a week","5 hours a day","none","an average of at least 60 minutes a day"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"According to Omar, what happens when we move?","answer":"More blood and oxygen flow to the brain.","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"يتدفق دم وأكسجين أكثر إلى الدماغ.","options":["We get more tired.","More blood and oxygen flow to the brain.","We forget our lessons.","Our eyes feel heavy."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What do *some people* say about exercise breaks?","answer":"They waste valuable lesson time.","explanation":"Paragraph 5.","explanation_ar":"تضيّع وقت الدرس.","options":["They are too short.","They are too easy.","They waste valuable lesson time.","They should be one hour long."],"dok":2,"skill":"counterargument","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How does Omar answer the other side?","answer":"A short break helps focused students learn more in the rest of the lesson.","explanation":"However, …","explanation_ar":"الاستراحة القصيرة تزيد التركيز.","options":["A short break helps focused students learn more in the rest of the lesson.","He agrees that breaks waste time.","He says lessons should be shorter.","He ignores it."],"dok":2,"skill":"counterargument","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS3-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Purpose and point of view. Choose.","instructions_ar":"الهدف ووجهة النظر: اختر.","items":[{"q":"What is the MAIN purpose of *Every School Needs a Daily Exercise Break*?","answer":"to persuade","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"الإقناع.","options":["to entertain","to explain how sleep works","to describe a trip","to persuade"],"dok":1,"skill":"author's purpose","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What is the MAIN purpose of *The Science of Sleep*?","answer":"to inform and explain","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"الإعلام والشرح.","options":["to persuade schools to change","to inform and explain","to tell a funny story","to sell beds"],"dok":1,"skill":"author's purpose","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which words show Omar's point of view MOST strongly?","answer":"I strongly believe","explanation":"Opinion words.","explanation_ar":"أعتقد بشدة.","options":["more blood and oxygen","ten minutes","the last lesson","I strongly believe"],"dok":1,"skill":"point of view","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why does Omar include a fact from the World Health Organization?","answer":"to support his opinion with information from experts","explanation":"Facts support opinions.","explanation_ar":"ليدعم رأيه.","options":["to support his opinion with information from experts","to change the topic","to show he disagrees","to entertain the reader"],"dok":2,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence from the SLEEP article shows a NEUTRAL point of view?","answer":"Each cycle lasts about 90 minutes and has different stages.","explanation":"Neutral fact.","explanation_ar":"محايدة.","options":["I believe everyone should sleep more!","Let's all go to bed early!","Each cycle lasts about 90 minutes and has different stages.","Sleeping late is the worst habit ever."],"dok":2,"skill":"point of view","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How are the two authors' points of view ALIKE?","answer":"Both think healthy habits help students learn better.","explanation":"Compare.","explanation_ar":"كلاهما يرى أن العادات الصحية تساعد على التعلم.","options":["Both want longer school days.","Both think healthy habits help students learn better.","Both say screens are good.","Both write stories."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS3-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Complete the Author's Purpose & Point of View Chart.","instructions_ar":"أكمل جدول هدف الكاتب ووجهة نظره.","items":[{"q":"Purpose – what is the purpose of each text?","answer":"The sleep article informs and explains. Omar's text persuades.","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"الهدف.","dok":1,"skill":"author's purpose","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Point of view – neutral or a strong opinion?","answer":"The sleep article is neutral. Omar has a strong opinion in favor of exercise breaks.","explanation":"Point of view.","explanation_ar":"وجهة النظر.","dok":2,"skill":"point of view","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Evidence words – copy two from each text.","answer":"Sleep article: 'scientists know', 'experts recommend'. Omar: 'I believe', 'Let's get moving!'","explanation":"Evidence.","explanation_ar":"الدليل.","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer"},{"q":"What does each author want the reader to know or do?","answer":"The sleep author wants us to understand sleep and sleep better. Omar wants us to agree and start daily exercise breaks.","explanation":"Reader action.","explanation_ar":"ما يريده من القارئ.","dok":2,"skill":"author's purpose","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS3-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Respond and compare.","instructions_ar":"استجب وقارن.","items":[{"q":"Do you agree with Omar? Give one reason and one fact.","answer":"Yes. Moving helps us concentrate, and the WHO recommends 60 minutes of activity a day.","explanation":"Opinion + fact.","explanation_ar":"رأي + حقيقة.","dok":2,"skill":"point of view","stage":"production"},{"q":"Rewrite Omar's first sentence of paragraph 3 in a NEUTRAL way.","answer":"The World Health Organization recommends an average of at least 60 minutes of physical activity a day for children and teenagers.","explanation":"Neutral rewrite.","explanation_ar":"إعادة صياغة محايدة.","dok":3,"skill":"point of view","stage":"production"},{"q":"How could the sleep article's author write a PERSUASIVE sentence about screens?","answer":"I strongly believe that every student should put away screens an hour before bed!","explanation":"Persuasive rewrite.","explanation_ar":"إعادة صياغة إقناعية.","dok":3,"skill":"point of view","stage":"production"},{"q":"Which text changed YOUR mind more? Why?","answer":"Omar's text, because he spoke to me directly and gave reasons I could feel in my own day.","explanation":"Evaluate.","explanation_ar":"قيّم.","dok":3,"skill":"evaluate","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS3-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"Every School Needs a Daily Exercise Break (by Omar)\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “Every School Needs a Daily Exercise Break (by Omar)”.","answer":"218 words","title":"Every School Needs a Daily Exercise Break (by Omar)","body":"Imagine sitting still at your desk for six hours. By the last lesson, your back hurts, your eyes feel heavy and the teacher's words float past you. I believe every school should give students a ten-minute exercise break every day.\n\nFirst, exercise helps us learn. When we move, more blood and oxygen flow to the brain. Many teachers notice that students concentrate better after a short activity break. For example, after our PE lessons, our class always answers more questions in math.\n\nSecond, an exercise break is good for our health. The World Health Organization recommends that children and teenagers do an average of at least 60 minutes of physical activity every day. A daily break would give us part of that time at school.\n\nThird, moving together reduces stress. After a difficult test, a few minutes of stretching or jumping can help us relax and feel happier. It also gives friends a chance to laugh together.\n\nSome people say that exercise breaks waste valuable lesson time. However, a ten-minute break is short, and focused students may learn more in the rest of the lesson than tired students learn in a full one.\n\nFor these reasons, I strongly believe that every school needs a daily exercise break. Let's get moving – our bodies and our brains will thank us!","words":218,"limit":145}],"time_limit_sec":145},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS3-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Author's Purpose & Point of View Chart","instructions":"Organizer: Complete each row for both texts.","items":[{"q":"Purpose (inform, explain, persuade?)","answer":"Sleep article: to inform and explain · Omar: to persuade"},{"q":"Point of view (neutral or strong opinion?)","answer":"Sleep article: neutral · Omar: a strong opinion for exercise breaks"},{"q":"Evidence words","answer":"Sleep article: 'scientists know', 'experts recommend', numbers · Omar: 'I believe', 'should', 'strongly', 'Let's get moving!'"},{"q":"What does the author want the reader to do or know?","answer":"Sleep article: understand how sleep works and sleep better · Omar: agree and add a daily exercise break"}]}],"game":{"name":"Purpose Target Practice","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Target range: an extract flies in; the child taps the purpose ring, then chooses 'neutral' or 'strong opinion' and the evidence word. Correct answers hit the bullseye.","A player reads an extract card aloud.","The team decides the purpose and places a sticky dart on the target.","The team names the point of view (neutral or strong opinion) and the evidence words.","Other teams challenge if they disagree.","Correct purpose = 1 point; correct point of view with evidence = 2 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is an author's *purpose*?","answer":"the reason the author wrote the text","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"سبب الكتابة.","options":["the title of the text","the reason the author wrote the text","the last sentence","the number of pages"],"dok":1,"skill":"author's purpose"},{"q":"Which word shows an OPINION?","answer":"should","explanation":"Opinion word.","explanation_ar":"should.","options":["minutes","should","oxygen","cycle"],"dok":1,"skill":"point of view"},{"q":"*The science article has a **neutral** tone.* *Neutral* means ___.","answer":"not taking a side","explanation":"Neutral.","explanation_ar":"محايد.","options":["very angry","very funny","very sad","not taking a side"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"What does *Let's get moving!* show?","answer":"a call to action","explanation":"Persuasive ending.","explanation_ar":"دعوة للعمل.","options":["a neutral fact","a counterargument","a call to action","a definition"],"dok":1,"skill":"persuasive techniques"},{"q":"Which sentence about Omar's view is correct?","answer":"Omar believes that schools should give exercise breaks.","explanation":"believes + should + verb.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Omar believes that schools should give exercise breaks.","Omar believe that schools should give exercise breaks.","Omar believes that schools should to give exercise breaks.","Omar believing that schools should give exercise breaks."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Why does Omar begin with *Imagine sitting still at your desk for six hours*?","answer":"to help the reader feel the problem","explanation":"Hook.","explanation_ar":"ليشعر القارئ بالمشكلة.","options":["to give a scientific fact","to tell a fairy tale","to help the reader feel the problem","to describe his school building"],"dok":2,"skill":"author's craft"},{"q":"Which part of Omar's text answers the OTHER side?","answer":"Some people say … However, …","explanation":"Counterargument.","explanation_ar":"الرد على الرأي الآخر.","options":["First, exercise helps us learn.","Imagine sitting still…","Let's get moving!","Some people say … However, …"],"dok":2,"skill":"counterargument"},{"q":"Which phrase tells you the sleep article uses EXPERT information?","answer":"experts recommend","explanation":"Expert source.","explanation_ar":"الخبراء يوصون.","options":["experts recommend","I strongly believe","Let's","Imagine"],"dok":2,"skill":"point of view"},{"q":"How are the purposes of the two texts DIFFERENT?","answer":"One explains how sleep works; the other tries to persuade schools to add exercise breaks.","explanation":"Contrast.","explanation_ar":"أحدهما يشرح والآخر يُقنع.","options":["One explains how sleep works; the other tries to persuade schools to add exercise breaks.","Both tell stories.","Both persuade readers to buy something.","Both explain how to play sports."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts"},{"q":"A text says: *Every family must stop using phones at dinner – it is the only way to be happy!* What is TRUE about it?","answer":"It shows a strong opinion and wants to persuade.","explanation":"Apply.","explanation_ar":"رأي قوي وهدفه الإقناع.","options":["It is neutral and gives only facts.","It is a science explanation.","It shows a strong opinion and wants to persuade.","It is a story."],"dok":3,"skill":"point of view"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'purpose': a target with an arrow"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'persuade': a child convincing a teacher"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'point of view': two children looking at the same thing from different sides"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'oxygen': an O₂ symbol with air bubbles"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'physical activity': children playing a running game"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'valuable': a clock with a gold star"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'neutral': a balance scale with equal sides"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-01","prompt":"Students taking an exercise break in class."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-02","prompt":"An author's purpose target."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS3-03","prompt":"Neutral facts and persuasive words."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V01","script":"purpose. The author's purpose is to persuade."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V02","script":"persuade. Omar wants to persuade the principal."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V03","script":"point of view. The author's point of view is clear in the first paragraph."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V04","script":"oxygen. Exercise sends more oxygen to the brain."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V05","script":"physical activity. Children need physical activity every day."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V06","script":"valuable. Lesson time is valuable."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-V07","script":"neutral. The science article has a neutral tone."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-T1","script":"Imagine sitting still at your desk for six hours. By the last lesson, your back hurts, your eyes feel heavy and the teacher's words float past you. I believe every school should give students a ten-minute exercise break every day. First, exercise helps us learn. When we move, more blood and oxygen flow to the brain. Many teachers notice that students concentrate better after a short activity break. For example, after our PE lessons, our class always answers more questions in math. Second, an exercise break is good for our health. The World Health Organization recommends that children and teenagers do an average of at least 60 minutes of physical activity every day. A daily break would give us part of that time at school. Third, moving together reduces stress. After a difficult test, a few minutes of stretching or jumping can help us relax and feel happier. It also gives friends a chance to laugh together. Some people say that exercise breaks waste valuable lesson time. However, a ten-minute break is short, and focused students may learn more in the rest of the lesson than tired students learn in a full one. For these reasons, I strongly believe that every school needs a daily exercise break. Let's get moving – our bodies and our brains will thank us!"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Why did the author write this? To inform, explain, persuade or entertain? Imagine sitting still at your desk for six hours… Opinion words show the author's point of view: I believe, should, strongly, Let's! The sleep article is neutral: facts, experts and research. Its purpose: to inform and explain. Both authors agree: healthy habits help you learn!"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS4","title":"Writing Skill: Supporting reasons with facts","lesson_type":"writing_skill","objectives":["support each reason in an opinion text with a fact, a number, an example or an expert source","use linking phrases: For example, According to, This shows that, This is important because","tell the difference between strong support and weak support (feelings only, made-up numbers)"],"objectives_ar":["دعم كل سبب في نص الرأي بحقيقة أو رقم أو مثال أو مصدر خبير.","استخدام عبارات الربط.","التمييز بين الدعم القوي والدعم الضعيف."],"success_criteria":["I can match a reason to a fact that supports it.","I can use at least two kinds of support (fact, number, example, expert).","I can explain why a piece of support is strong or weak."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع مطابقة السبب بالحقيقة التي تدعمه.","أستطيع استخدام نوعين على الأقل من الدعم.","أستطيع شرح لماذا يكون الدعم قويًا أو ضعيفًا."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"reason","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrizən/","definition":"why you think or believe something","arabic":"سبب","example":"Give a reason for your opinion.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"fact","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fækt/","definition":"something that is true and can be checked","arabic":"حقيقة","example":"It is a fact that water boils at 100 °C.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"statistic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/stəˈtɪstɪk/","definition":"a number that gives information about something","arabic":"إحصائية","example":"The statistic shows that most students like sport.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"dehydration","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌdihaɪˈdreɪʃən/","definition":"not having enough water in your body","arabic":"الجفاف (نقص الماء في الجسم)","example":"Dehydration can cause headaches.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"refill","pos":"verb","ipa":"/riˈfɪl/","definition":"to fill something again","arabic":"يعيد التعبئة","example":"Refill your bottle at the water station.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"source","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɔrs/","definition":"where information comes from (a person, a book, a website)","arabic":"مصدر","example":"Name the source of your fact.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"reliable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rɪˈlaɪəbəl/","definition":"able to be trusted","arabic":"موثوق","example":"The WHO is a reliable source about health.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"An **opinion** needs **reasons**, and every reason needs **support**. Without support, a reason is just a feeling. Strong writers use four kinds of support: **facts** (true information), **numbers/statistics**, **examples** (from life or experience) and **expert sources** (doctors, scientists, the World Health Organization).\n\nUse **linking phrases** to add support: *For example, …* / *According to [source], …* / *Studies show that …* / *This is important because …* / *This shows that …*.\n\nCheck your support: Is it **true**? Is it from a **reliable source**? Does it really **connect** to your reason? Avoid **weak support** like made-up numbers (*100 percent of students…*) or feelings only (*because I think it's nice*).","examples":["Reason: *Water helps our brains work well.* → Fact: ***More than half of the human body is water.***","Reason: *Our weather is very hot.* → Number: ***In many Saudi cities, summer temperatures rise above 40 °C.***","Reason: *Students need easier access to water.* → Example: ***After our sports lesson, the line at the only fountain took ten minutes!***","Reason: *Children need more activity.* → Expert: ***According to the World Health Organization, children should be active for an average of at least 60 minutes a day.***","Explaining the support: ***This is important because tired students can't concentrate.***","Weak (feeling only): *Water stations are good because I like them.*","Weak (made-up number): *Water stations make students 1,000 times smarter.*","Weak (doesn't connect): *Water stations are good because the sea is blue.*","Strong paragraph pattern: **Reason → support (fact/number/example/expert) → explain why it matters.**"],"common_errors":["✗ Giving reasons with no support. → ✓ Add a fact, a number, an example or an expert. (Every reason needs support.)","✗ Making up numbers. → ✓ Use real facts from reliable sources. (Be honest.)","✗ Support that doesn't match the reason. → ✓ Check: does this fact prove THIS reason? (Connect it.)","✗ According the doctors… → ✓ According to doctors… (**according to**.)","✗ For example students drink… → ✓ For example, students drink… (Comma after **For example**.)","✗ Dehydration it causes headaches. → ✓ Dehydration causes headaches. (No extra subject.)","✗ This is important because of tired students can't… → ✓ This is important because tired students can't… (**because** + sentence.)"],"arabic":"الرأي يحتاج إلى أسباب، وكل سبب يحتاج إلى دعم؛ وإلا صار مجرد شعور. أنواع الدعم: حقائق، أرقام وإحصاءات، أمثلة، مصادر خبيرة.\n\nاستخدم عبارات الربط: For example, According to, Studies show that, This is important because.\n\nتحقق من الدعم: هل هو صحيح؟ هل مصدره موثوق؟ هل يرتبط بالسبب فعلًا؟ وتجنب الأرقام المختلقة والمشاعر وحدها.\n\nنمط الفقرة القوية: سبب ← دعم ← شرح أهميته."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"\"Water stations are good because I like them.\" Hmm… is that convincing? Let's make it stronger!","on_screen":"Supporting Reasons with Facts 💧📊","visual":"A weak sentence wobbles on a thin stick; a strong one stands on four pillars."},{"time":"00:25–01:25","narration":"Do you ever feel tired or get a headache in the afternoon?…","on_screen":"(Layla's model)","visual":"Layla with a water bottle; a thermometer at 40 °C; a long line at a fountain."},{"time":"01:25–02:25","narration":"Four kinds of support: facts, numbers, examples and experts!","on_screen":"Fact · Number · Example · Expert","visual":"Four pillars labelled with icons hold up a sign saying 'REASON'."},{"time":"02:25–03:05","narration":"Weak support: feelings only, made-up numbers, facts that don't connect. Strong support: true, reliable and connected!","on_screen":"Weak ❌ / Strong ✅","visual":"A '1,000 times smarter!' sign cracks and falls."},{"time":"03:05–03:30","narration":"Reason → support → explain why it matters. Now your opinion stands strong!","on_screen":"Reason → Support → Why","visual":"Three steps light up."}],"captions_ar":["«محطات الماء جيدة لأنني أحبها»… هل هذا مقنع؟ لنجعله أقوى!","هل تشعر بالتعب أو الصداع بعد الظهر؟…","أربعة أنواع من الدعم: حقائق وأرقام وأمثلة وخبراء!","الدعم الضعيف: مشاعر فقط أو أرقام مختلقة أو حقائق لا ترتبط. الدعم القوي: صحيح وموثوق ومرتبط!","سبب ← دعم ← شرح الأهمية. الآن يقف رأيك قويًا!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, clear female teacher, speed 0.95. Layla reads her model."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Every Classroom Should Have a Water Station (by Layla)","body":"Do you ever feel tired or get a headache in the afternoon? You might simply be thirsty. I believe every classroom should have a water station where students can refill their bottles at any time.\n\nMy first reason is that water helps our brains work well. More than half of the human body is water, and even mild dehydration can cause tiredness and headaches. My second reason is our hot weather. In many Saudi cities, summer temperatures rise above 40 °C, so students lose water quickly when they play outside. For example, after our sports lesson last week, the line at the only water fountain took ten minutes! Finally, refillable bottles reduce plastic waste. A water station in every classroom would keep us healthy, focused and kind to the planet.","word_count":130,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L05-U2-LS4-1","genre":"model text","role":"model","difficulty":"550L–750L","glossary":[],"annotations":["**Hook + opinion:** a question about a real problem, then *I believe every classroom should…*","**Reason 1 + fact:** *water helps our brains work well* ← *More than half of the human body is water … mild dehydration can cause tiredness and headaches.*","**Reason 2 + number:** *our hot weather* ← *summer temperatures rise above 40 °C* (a statistic).","**Example:** *For example, after our sports lesson last week, the line … took ten minutes!* – a personal example makes the reason real.","**Reason 3 + effect:** *refillable bottles reduce plastic waste*.","**Linking words:** *My first reason, My second reason, For example, Finally, so*.","**Concluding sentence:** repeats the opinion with three benefits: *healthy, focused and kind to the planet*."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Layla's model. Choose the best answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ نموذج ليلى واختر أفضل إجابة.","items":[{"q":"What is Layla's opinion about water in classrooms?","answer":"Every classroom should have a water station.","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"يجب أن يكون في كل فصل محطة ماء.","options":["Students should drink less water.","Every classroom should have a water station.","Schools should close in summer.","Water fountains are too fast."],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How does Layla begin her text?","answer":"with a question about a real problem","explanation":"Hook.","explanation_ar":"بسؤال.","options":["with a list of numbers","with a story about a camel","with a question about a real problem","with her name"],"dok":1,"skill":"hooks","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which FACT supports the reason that water helps our brains?","answer":"Even mild dehydration can cause tiredness and headaches.","explanation":"Fact → reason.","explanation_ar":"الجفاف البسيط يسبب التعب والصداع.","options":["Even mild dehydration can cause tiredness and headaches.","The line took ten minutes.","Bottles reduce plastic.","Summer temperatures rise above 40 °C."],"dok":2,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which NUMBER does Layla use?","answer":"above 40 °C","explanation":"Statistic.","explanation_ar":"أعلى من 40 درجة.","options":["100 percent","above 40 °C","1,000 times","six hours"],"dok":1,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What kind of support is *after our sports lesson last week, the line … took ten minutes*?","answer":"a personal example","explanation":"Example.","explanation_ar":"مثال شخصي.","options":["an expert source","a statistic from a study","a feeling only","a personal example"],"dok":2,"skill":"types of support","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What are the three benefits in Layla's concluding sentence?","answer":"healthy, focused and kind to the planet","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"صحة وتركيز ورفق بالكوكب.","options":["fast, cheap and new","cold, sweet and fun","healthy, focused and kind to the planet","quiet, clean and big"],"dok":1,"skill":"conclusions","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS4-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Strong and weak support. Choose.","instructions_ar":"الدعم القوي والضعيف: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Reason: *Children need more physical activity.* Which is the STRONGEST support?","answer":"According to the World Health Organization, children should be active for an average of at least 60 minutes a day.","explanation":"Expert source.","explanation_ar":"الأقوى.","options":["I think running is fun.","Activity makes you 500 times stronger.","My cousin has a bike.","According to the World Health Organization, children should be active for an average of at least 60 minutes a day."],"dok":2,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which support for healthy school snacks is WEAK?","answer":"Healthy snacks are good because I like apples.","explanation":"Feeling only.","explanation_ar":"دعم ضعيف.","options":["Fruit has vitamins that help the body fight germs.","Sugary drinks can damage teeth.","Healthy snacks are good because I like apples.","Doctors recommend eating fruit and vegetables every day."],"dok":2,"skill":"weak support","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which support does NOT connect to the reason *Sleep helps students learn*?","answer":"Camels can walk for days without water.","explanation":"Not connected.","explanation_ar":"لا يرتبط.","options":["Camels can walk for days without water.","Scientists believe REM sleep helps store memories.","Tired students find it hard to concentrate.","Experts recommend 9 to 12 hours for children."],"dok":2,"skill":"weak support","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which linking phrase introduces an EXPERT source?","answer":"According to","explanation":"Linking phrase.","explanation_ar":"According to.","options":["According to","For example","Finally","However"],"dok":1,"skill":"linking phrases","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about doctors' advice is written correctly?","answer":"According to doctors, children should drink water often.","explanation":"according to + comma.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["According doctors, children should drink water often.","According to doctors children should to drink water often.","According for doctors, children should drink water often.","According to doctors, children should drink water often."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why should you EXPLAIN your support after giving it?","answer":"to show the reader how the fact proves your reason","explanation":"Reason → support → why.","explanation_ar":"لتُظهر كيف يثبت الدعمُ السببَ.","options":["to make the paragraph longer","to show the reader how the fact proves your reason","to change your opinion","to add a joke"],"dok":3,"skill":"explaining evidence","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS4-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the supported reasons with the word bank.","instructions_ar":"أكمل الأسباب المدعومة من بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"________ the World Health Organization, children should be active every day.","answer":"According to","explanation":"Expert source.","explanation_ar":"وفقًا لـ.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Students get thirsty quickly. ________, after sports, many students feel dizzy.","answer":"For example","explanation":"Example.","explanation_ar":"على سبيل المثال.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Fruit contains vitamins. ________ because vitamins help our bodies fight germs.","answer":"This is important","explanation":"Explain.","explanation_ar":"هذا مهم.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Even mild ________ can cause tiredness and headaches.","answer":"dehydration","explanation":"Fact.","explanation_ar":"الجفاف.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"A ________ source, such as a doctor or a science book, can be trusted.","answer":"reliable","explanation":"Trusted.","explanation_ar":"موثوق.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"A ________, such as '40 °C', gives a number as support.","answer":"statistic","explanation":"Number.","explanation_ar":"إحصائية.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS4-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Add support to reasons.","instructions_ar":"أضف الدعم إلى الأسباب.","items":[{"q":"Add a FACT to this reason: *Schools should serve fruit at break time.*","answer":"Fruit contains vitamins and fiber that help the body stay healthy.","explanation":"Fact.","explanation_ar":"حقيقة.","dok":2,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"production"},{"q":"Add a personal EXAMPLE to this reason: *Students need a quiet place to relax.*","answer":"For example, after our hard math test, many of us felt stressed and wanted a calm corner to read.","explanation":"Example.","explanation_ar":"مثال.","dok":2,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"production"},{"q":"Add an EXPERT source and explain why it matters: *Children should sleep more.*","answer":"According to sleep experts, children aged 6 to 12 need 9 to 12 hours a night. This is important because tired students can't concentrate.","explanation":"Expert + explain.","explanation_ar":"خبير + شرح.","dok":3,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"production"},{"q":"Fix this weak support: *Exercise breaks are good because 100 percent of students love them.*","answer":"Exercise breaks are good because moving sends more oxygen to the brain, which helps students concentrate.","explanation":"Revise.","explanation_ar":"حسّن.","dok":3,"skill":"revising","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Pillars of Proof","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Build it: the child places an opinion roof on reasons, then holds each reason up with a support pillar. Weak pillars (feelings, made-up numbers) crack and must be replaced.","Each team gets an opinion card and three reason cards.","They choose a strong support card for each reason.","They explain each choice with 'This shows that…'.","Other teams try to 'knock down' weak pillars by finding problems.","Each strong pillar = 2 points; each weak pillar found by another team = 1 point for that team."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What does a *reason* need to be convincing?","answer":"support, such as a fact, a number, an example or an expert","explanation":"Support.","explanation_ar":"دعم.","options":["a long title","many exclamation marks","a funny picture","support, such as a fact, a number, an example or an expert"],"dok":1,"skill":"supporting evidence"},{"q":"Which is a FACT?","answer":"Water boils at 100 °C at sea level.","explanation":"Fact vs. opinion.","explanation_ar":"حقيقة.","options":["Water tastes the best.","Water boils at 100 °C at sea level.","Everyone loves swimming.","Summer is the worst season."],"dok":1,"skill":"facts"},{"q":"*Name the **source** of your fact.* *Source* means ___.","answer":"where the information comes from","explanation":"Source.","explanation_ar":"المصدر.","options":["the end of the paragraph","a kind of drink","the main idea","where the information comes from"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which phrase introduces an EXAMPLE?","answer":"For example,","explanation":"Linking phrase.","explanation_ar":"For example.","options":["According to","In conclusion,","For example,","However,"],"dok":1,"skill":"linking phrases"},{"q":"Which sentence with a linking phrase is punctuated correctly?","answer":"For example, many students feel tired after lunch.","explanation":"Comma after For example.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["For example many students feel tired after lunch.","For example, many students feel tired after lunch.","For, example many students feel tired after lunch.","For example many, students feel tired after lunch."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation"},{"q":"Which support is from a RELIABLE source?","answer":"The World Health Organization recommends 60 minutes of activity a day.","explanation":"Reliable source.","explanation_ar":"مصدر موثوق.","options":["My friend said exercise is boring.","A cartoon said juice is healthier than water.","The World Health Organization recommends 60 minutes of activity a day.","Someone online said sleep is a waste of time."],"dok":2,"skill":"reliable sources"},{"q":"Why is *Water stations make students 1,000 times smarter* WEAK support?","answer":"It is a made-up number that is not true.","explanation":"Made-up statistic.","explanation_ar":"رقم مختلق.","options":["It is too short.","It uses a comma.","It is a made-up number that is not true.","It names an expert."],"dok":2,"skill":"weak support"},{"q":"Which is the best order for a strong supported reason?","answer":"reason → support → explain why it matters","explanation":"Pattern.","explanation_ar":"سبب ← دعم ← شرح.","options":["support → title → reason","reason → support → explain why it matters","explain → opinion → hook","example → question → title"],"dok":2,"skill":"organization"},{"q":"Reason: *Screens before bed are a problem.* Which support connects BEST?","answer":"Blue light from screens makes the body produce less melatonin, so it is harder to fall asleep.","explanation":"Connected support.","explanation_ar":"الدعم المرتبط.","options":["Blue light from screens makes the body produce less melatonin, so it is harder to fall asleep.","Screens come in many colors.","My tablet was expensive.","Phones can take photos."],"dok":3,"skill":"supporting evidence"},{"q":"A classmate writes: *Healthy food is good because it is good.* What is the BEST advice?","answer":"Add a fact or an example that shows why healthy food helps your body.","explanation":"Revising.","explanation_ar":"أضف حقيقة أو مثالًا.","options":["Add a fact or an example that shows why healthy food helps your body.","Write it again in capital letters.","Add three exclamation marks.","Make the sentence shorter."],"dok":3,"skill":"revising"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'reason': a thought bubble with 'because…'"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'fact': a checkmark next to a book"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'statistic': a bar chart"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'dehydration': a tired child with an empty bottle"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'refill': a bottle being refilled at a tap"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'source': a book and a website icon"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'reliable': a shield with a checkmark"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-01","prompt":"Layla refilling a bottle at a classroom water station."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-02","prompt":"Four kinds of support for a reason."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS4-03","prompt":"Weak support and strong support."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V01","script":"reason. Give a reason for your opinion."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V02","script":"fact. It is a fact that water boils at 100 °C."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V03","script":"statistic. The statistic shows that most students like sport."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V04","script":"dehydration. Dehydration can cause headaches."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V05","script":"refill. Refill your bottle at the water station."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V06","script":"source. Name the source of your fact."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-V07","script":"reliable. The WHO is a reliable source about health."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-T1","script":"Do you ever feel tired or get a headache in the afternoon? You might simply be thirsty. I believe every classroom should have a water station where students can refill their bottles at any time. My first reason is that water helps our brains work well. More than half of the human body is water, and even mild dehydration can cause tiredness and headaches. My second reason is our hot weather. In many Saudi cities, summer temperatures rise above 40 °C, so students lose water quickly when they play outside. For example, after our sports lesson last week, the line at the only water fountain took ten minutes! Finally, refillable bottles reduce plastic waste. A water station in every classroom would keep us healthy, focused and kind to the planet."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS4-VID","script":"\"Water stations are good because I like them.\" Hmm… is that convincing? Let's make it stronger! Do you ever feel tired or get a headache in the afternoon?… Four kinds of support: facts, numbers, examples and experts! Weak support: feelings only, made-up numbers, facts that don't connect. Strong support: true, reliable and connected! Reason → support → explain why it matters. Now your opinion stands strong!"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS5","title":"Writing Workshop: A two-paragraph opinion text on a healthy-school rule","lesson_type":"writing_workshop","objectives":["plan a two-paragraph opinion text about a healthy-school rule with the Opinion Planner","write 120–150 words with a hook, a clear opinion, two supported reasons, a counterargument and a conclusion","revise, edit and present the opinion to the class 'Healthy School Council'"],"objectives_ar":["التخطيط لنص رأي من فقرتين عن قاعدة مدرسية صحية بمخطط الرأي.","كتابة 120–150 كلمة فيها جملة جذب ورأي واضح وسببان مدعومان ورأي مخالف وخاتمة.","تحسين النص وتدقيقه وعرضه على «مجلس المدرسة الصحية» في الصف."],"success_criteria":["Paragraph 1 has a hook and a clear opinion.","Paragraph 2 has two reasons, each supported by a fact, a number, an example or an expert.","I answered the other side and wrote a strong conclusion in 120–150 words."],"success_criteria_ar":["الفقرة الأولى فيها جملة جذب ورأي واضح.","الفقرة الثانية فيها سببان مدعومان بحقيقة أو رقم أو مثال أو خبير.","رددت على الرأي الآخر وكتبت خاتمة قوية في 120–150 كلمة."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"rule","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rul/","definition":"something that says what people must or must not do","arabic":"قاعدة","example":"Our school has a new healthy rule.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"sugary","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈʃʊɡəri/","definition":"containing a lot of sugar","arabic":"سكري / كثير السكر","example":"Sugary drinks can damage teeth.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"acid","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈæsɪd/","definition":"a chemical that can damage things, like teeth","arabic":"حمض","example":"Germs make acid that damages teeth.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"fiber","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfaɪbər/","definition":"the part of plant food that helps your body digest food","arabic":"ألياف","example":"Vegetables have lots of fiber.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"replace","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈpleɪs/","definition":"to put something new in the place of something else","arabic":"يستبدل","example":"Replace soda with water.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"counterargument","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkaʊntərˌɑrɡjəmənt/","definition":"the opposite opinion that some people have","arabic":"الرأي المخالف / الحجة المضادة","example":"Answer the counterargument with a reason.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"council","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkaʊnsəl/","definition":"a group of people chosen to make decisions","arabic":"مجلس","example":"The student council will vote on the rule.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"An **opinion text** tries to **persuade** the reader. It has a clear **opinion**, **reasons** with **support**, and a strong **conclusion**.\n\n**Paragraph 1 – introduction:** a **hook** (a surprising fact or a question) + your **opinion** (*I believe our school should …*). **Paragraph 2 – body and conclusion:** **Reason 1 + support**, **Reason 2 + support**, a **counterargument** (*Some people say …*) with your **answer** (*However, …*), and a **concluding sentence** that repeats your opinion in new words (*For these reasons, …*).\n\nUse **linking words**: *First, Second, For example, According to, However, For these reasons*. Keep it **120–150 words** and use a **polite, confident** tone – you are writing to the school council!","examples":["Hook (surprising fact): ***Did you know that one can of soda can contain about eight teaspoons of sugar?***","Opinion: ***I believe our school should not sell sugary drinks, and students should drink water or milk instead.***","Reason 1 + expert: ***First, sugary drinks are bad for our teeth. According to dentists, sugar helps germs in the mouth make acid that damages teeth.***","Reason 2 + example: ***Second, these drinks give us quick energy that doesn't last. For example, after a soda at break, many of my classmates feel tired in the next lesson.***","Counterargument: ***Some people say students should be free to choose their own drinks.***","Answer: ***However, a school's job is to help students stay healthy and learn well.***","Conclusion: ***For these reasons, I strongly believe our school should replace sugary drinks with water and milk.***","Polite tone: *should, I believe, I suggest* – not *Stupid soda must go now!!!*","Paragraph break: start Paragraph 2 at *First, …*"],"common_errors":["✗ No clear opinion in Paragraph 1. → ✓ Write: I believe our school should … (Say what you think.)","✗ Reasons with no support. → ✓ Add a fact, a number, an example or an expert. (Support every reason.)","✗ Ignoring the other side. → ✓ Add 'Some people say … However, …'. (Answer the counterargument.)","✗ Rude tone: Soda is stupid! → ✓ Sugary drinks can harm our teeth. (Polite and confident.)","✗ The conclusion repeats the hook word for word. → ✓ Repeat your opinion in new words. (Fresh words.)","✗ Our school should to stop selling soda. → ✓ Our school should stop selling soda. (should + verb.)","✗ Replace soda by water. → ✓ Replace soda with water. (replace … **with** …)"],"arabic":"نص الرأي يحاول إقناع القارئ؛ فيه رأي واضح وأسباب مدعومة وخاتمة قوية.\n\nالفقرة الأولى: جملة جذب (حقيقة مدهشة أو سؤال) + رأيك. الفقرة الثانية: سبب أول + دعم، سبب ثانٍ + دعم، رأي مخالف مع الرد عليه، ثم جملة ختامية تعيد رأيك بكلمات جديدة.\n\nاستخدم كلمات الربط واكتب بنبرة مهذبة واثقة، والتزم بطول 120–150 كلمة.\n\nانتبه: should + الفعل دون to، وreplace … with …"},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:25","narration":"The Healthy School Council is listening! Which new rule will you suggest?","on_screen":"My Healthy-School Rule 🏫🥦","visual":"Students sit around a council table; Noura stands with notes."},{"time":"00:25–01:05","narration":"Read the rule cards: no sugary drinks, fruit in every lunch box, screen-free lunch, a calm corner.","on_screen":"Rule Cards A–D","visual":"Four cards appear with icons: a soda can, an apple, a phone with a cross, cushions."},{"time":"01:05–02:10","narration":"Did you know that one can of soda can contain about eight teaspoons of sugar?…","on_screen":"(model opinion text)","visual":"Eight sugar cubes drop next to a can; a tooth with germs; a tired student after break."},{"time":"02:10–03:00","narration":"Paragraph 1: hook + opinion. Paragraph 2: two supported reasons, the other side and a conclusion!","on_screen":"P1: Hook + Opinion · P2: Reasons + Counter + Conclusion","visual":"Two blocks build with labels and linking words."},{"time":"03:00–03:30","narration":"Be polite, be confident and use facts. Now present to the council!","on_screen":"Present your rule 🎤","visual":"The council votes with raised hands."}],"captions_ar":["مجلس المدرسة الصحية يستمع! أي قاعدة جديدة ستقترح؟","اقرأ بطاقات القواعد: لا مشروبات سكرية، فاكهة في كل علبة غداء، غداء بلا شاشات، ركن هادئ.","هل تعلم أن علبة مشروب غازي واحدة قد تحتوي على نحو ثماني ملاعق صغيرة من السكر؟…","الفقرة الأولى: جذب + رأي. الفقرة الثانية: سببان مدعومان والرأي الآخر وخاتمة!","كن مهذبًا وواثقًا واستخدم الحقائق، ثم اعرض على المجلس!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, confident female presenter, speed 0.95. Noura reads the model as if speaking to the school council."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Healthy-School Rule Cards","body":"**Card A – No sugary drinks at school** · Fact: one can of soda can contain about eight teaspoons of sugar · Fact: dentists say sugar helps germs in the mouth make acid that damages teeth · Example: students feel tired soon after a sugary drink at break\n\n**Card B – Fruit or vegetables in every lunch box** · Fact: fruit and vegetables have vitamins and fiber · Expert: the World Health Organization recommends eating at least 400 grams of fruit and vegetables a day · Example: an apple or carrot sticks are easy to carry\n\n**Card C – Screen-free lunch breaks** · Fact: talking and playing with friends helps build friendships · Fact: looking at screens for a long time can tire your eyes · Example: students who play outside at lunch come back more active\n\n**Card D – A calm corner in every classroom** · Fact: slow, deep breathing can help the body feel calm · Fact: short rests can reduce stress before tests · Example: a quiet corner with cushions and books helps students relax for a few minutes","word_count":166,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L05-U2-LS5-1","genre":"rule cards","role":"model","difficulty":"550L–750L","glossary":[],"annotations":["Choose **one rule** you agree with.","Use **at least two facts or examples** from the card (or other reliable facts you know).","Add a **counterargument** (Some people say …) and **answer** it (However, …)."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS5-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the rule cards and the model. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ البطاقات والنموذج واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"About how much sugar can one can of soda contain, according to Card A?","answer":"about eight teaspoons","explanation":"Card A.","explanation_ar":"نحو ثماني ملاعق صغيرة.","options":["about one teaspoon","about twenty cups","no sugar","about eight teaspoons"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How much fruit and vegetables does the WHO recommend a day (Card B)?","answer":"at least 400 grams","explanation":"Card B.","explanation_ar":"400 غرام على الأقل.","options":["at least 4 grams","at least 4 kilograms","at least 400 grams","none"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which card suggests a quiet place with cushions and books?","answer":"Card D – A calm corner","explanation":"Card D.","explanation_ar":"الركن الهادئ.","options":["Card D – A calm corner","Card A – No sugary drinks","Card B – Fruit in lunch boxes","Card C – Screen-free lunch"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"In the model, what do dentists say sugar helps germs do?","answer":"make acid that damages teeth","explanation":"Reason 1.","explanation_ar":"تكوين حمض يتلف الأسنان.","options":["make acid that damages teeth","clean teeth","grow hair","make bones strong"],"dok":1,"skill":"supporting evidence","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which counterargument does the model include?","answer":"Students should be free to choose their own drinks.","explanation":"Counterargument.","explanation_ar":"حرية الاختيار.","options":["Water is too expensive.","Milk tastes bad.","Teeth are not important.","Students should be free to choose their own drinks."],"dok":2,"skill":"counterargument","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How does the writer answer the counterargument?","answer":"A school's job is to help students stay healthy and learn well.","explanation":"However, …","explanation_ar":"مهمة المدرسة صحة الطلاب وتعلمهم.","options":["Students can drink soda at home.","A school's job is to help students stay healthy and learn well.","Soda is cheap.","Nobody likes water."],"dok":2,"skill":"counterargument","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS5-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Plan the opinion text. Choose.","instructions_ar":"خطّط لنص الرأي: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which is the BEST hook for Card B (fruit in every lunch box)?","answer":"Did you know that the WHO recommends at least 400 grams of fruit and vegetables a day?","explanation":"Fact hook.","explanation_ar":"الأفضل.","options":["Did you know that the WHO recommends at least 400 grams of fruit and vegetables a day?","I like apples.","This text is about fruit.","Fruit."],"dok":1,"skill":"hooks","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence states a CLEAR opinion about screen-free lunch breaks?","answer":"I believe our school should make lunch breaks screen-free.","explanation":"Opinion.","explanation_ar":"رأي واضح.","options":["Some students have phones.","I believe our school should make lunch breaks screen-free.","Lunch is at twelve.","Screens are made of glass."],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which support for Card D (a calm corner) is an EXAMPLE?","answer":"After our hard science test, I sat in a quiet corner for three minutes and felt calm again.","explanation":"Example.","explanation_ar":"مثال.","options":["Slow breathing can help the body feel calm.","Experts say rest reduces stress.","Stress is a feeling.","After our hard science test, I sat in a quiet corner for three minutes and felt calm again."],"dok":2,"skill":"types of support","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which counterargument and answer fit Card C (screen-free lunch)?","answer":"Some people say phones help students relax. However, playing with friends helps us relax and build friendships.","explanation":"Counter + answer.","explanation_ar":"الأنسب.","options":["Phones are expensive. However, lunch is short.","Some people like pizza. However, I like rice.","Some people say phones help students relax. However, playing with friends helps us relax and build friendships.","Screens are bright. However, the sun is bright too."],"dok":3,"skill":"counterargument","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Where should Paragraph 2 BEGIN?","answer":"at the first reason (First, …)","explanation":"Paragraphing.","explanation_ar":"عند السبب الأول.","options":["at the hook","at the first reason (First, …)","at the conclusion","in the middle of the opinion sentence"],"dok":2,"skill":"paragraphing","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about the rule uses *replace* correctly?","answer":"Our school should replace sugary drinks with water.","explanation":"replace … with.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Our school should replace sugary drinks by water.","Our school should replace to water.","Our school should replacing sugary drinks with water.","Our school should replace sugary drinks with water."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS5-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Plan your opinion text with the Opinion Planner.","instructions_ar":"خطط لنص رأيك بمخطط الرأي.","items":[{"q":"Hook and opinion – write notes.","answer":"Hook: WHO recommends 400 g of fruit and vegetables a day. Opinion: every lunch box should include fruit or vegetables.","explanation":"Hook + opinion.","explanation_ar":"جذب + رأي.","dok":1,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Reason 1 + support – write notes.","answer":"vitamins and fiber keep the body healthy – fact from Card B","explanation":"Reason 1.","explanation_ar":"السبب 1.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Reason 2 + support – write notes.","answer":"easy to carry – example: an apple or carrot sticks fit in any bag","explanation":"Reason 2.","explanation_ar":"السبب 2.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Counterargument + answer + conclusion – write notes.","answer":"Some say: children don't like vegetables. However: there are many kinds to choose from. Conclusion: a small change for a healthier school.","explanation":"Counter + conclusion.","explanation_ar":"رأي مخالف + خاتمة.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS5-A4","type":"writing","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write, revise, edit and present your opinion text.","instructions_ar":"اكتب نص رأيك وحسّنه ودققه واعرضه.","items":[{"q":"Write Paragraph 1: your hook and opinion.","answer":"Did you know that the World Health Organization recommends at least 400 grams of fruit and vegetables a day? I believe every lunch box at our school should include fruit or vegetables.","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"الفقرة الأولى.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write your two reasons with support.","answer":"First, fruit and vegetables have vitamins and fiber that keep our bodies strong. Second, they are easy to bring. For example, an apple or a few carrot sticks fit in any school bag.","explanation":"Reasons.","explanation_ar":"الأسباب.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write your counterargument, your answer and your conclusion.","answer":"Some people say that children don't like vegetables. However, there are many kinds to choose from, such as cucumbers, grapes and dates. For these reasons, I strongly believe fruit and vegetables should be in every lunch box.","explanation":"Counter + conclusion.","explanation_ar":"رأي مخالف + خاتمة.","dok":3,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write one reason you made stronger after the Two-Partner Edit (before → after).","answer":"Before: Fruit is good. After: Fruit has vitamins and fiber that help our bodies stay healthy.","explanation":"Revision.","explanation_ar":"تحسين.","dok":3,"skill":"revising","stage":"production","_w":{"checklist":[],"min":null,"max":null}}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS5-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Opinion Planner","instructions":"Organizer: Use a rule card. Write short notes for each part.","items":[{"q":"Hook (surprising fact or question)","answer":"one can of soda ≈ eight teaspoons of sugar"},{"q":"Opinion (I believe our school should …)","answer":"school should not sell sugary drinks; water or milk instead"},{"q":"Reason 1 + support","answer":"bad for teeth – dentists: sugar helps germs make acid"},{"q":"Reason 2 + support","answer":"quick energy that doesn't last – example: classmates tired after soda at break"},{"q":"Counterargument + my answer","answer":"some say: free to choose · however: school's job is health and learning"},{"q":"Conclusion (opinion in new words)","answer":"replace sugary drinks with water and milk"}]},{"id":"RW-L05-U2-LS5-WR","type":"writing","instructions":"Writing: Choose a healthy-school rule card. Write a two-paragraph opinion text (120–150 words) for the school council. Paragraph 1: a hook and your opinion. Paragraph 2: two reasons with support, a counterargument with your answer, and a conclusion. Choose a healthy-school rule card. Write a two-paragraph opinion text (120–150 words) for the school council. Paragraph 1: a hook and your opinion. Paragraph 2: two reasons with support, a counterargument with your answer, and a conclusion.","instructions_ar":"اختر بطاقة قاعدة مدرسية صحية، واكتب نص رأي من فقرتين (120–150 كلمة) لمجلس المدرسة. الفقرة الأولى: جملة جذب ورأيك. الفقرة الثانية: سببان مدعومان ورأي مخالف مع ردك عليه وخاتمة.","prompt":"Choose a healthy-school rule card. Write a two-paragraph opinion text (120–150 words) for the school council. Paragraph 1: a hook and your opinion. Paragraph 2: two reasons with support, a counterargument with your answer, and a conclusion.","checklist":["My hook is a surprising fact or a question.","My opinion is clear (I believe our school should …).","I gave two reasons.","Each reason has support: a fact, a number, an example or an expert.","I wrote a counterargument and answered it with However.","My conclusion repeats my opinion in new words.","I used linking words and a polite, confident tone.","My text has two paragraphs and 120–150 words, and I checked spelling and punctuation."],"rubric_id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","min_words":120,"max_words":170,"organizer":"Opinion Planner (hook – opinion – reason 1 + support – reason 2 + support – counterargument + answer – conclusion)","items":[{"q":"Choose a healthy-school rule card. Write a two-paragraph opinion text (120–150 words) for the school council. Paragraph 1: a hook and your opinion. Paragraph 2: two reasons with support, a counterargument with your answer, and a conclusion.","answer":"Did you know that one can of soda can contain about eight teaspoons of sugar? I believe our school should not sell sugary drinks, and students should drink water or milk instead. (new paragraph) First, sugary drinks are bad for our teeth. According to dentists, sugar helps germs in the mouth make acid that damages teeth. Second, these drinks give us quick energy that doesn't last. For example, after a soda at break, many of my classmates feel tired in the next lesson. Some people say students should be free to choose their own drinks. However, a school's job is to help students stay healthy and learn well. For these reasons, I strongly believe our school should replace sugary drinks with water and milk.","_w":{"checklist":["My hook is a surprising fact or a question.","My opinion is clear (I believe our school should …).","I gave two reasons.","Each reason has support: a fact, a number, an example or an expert.","I wrote a counterargument and answered it with However.","My conclusion repeats my opinion in new words.","I used linking words and a polite, confident tone.","My text has two paragraphs and 120–150 words, and I checked spelling and punctuation."],"min":120,"max":170}}]}],"game":{"name":"Healthy School Council","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Council chamber: the child builds an opinion speech by choosing a hook, an opinion, two supported reasons, a counterargument and a conclusion. The virtual council votes; strong support earns more green votes.","Teams choose a rule and prepare a 60-second speech using their opinion texts.","Each team presents to the council (the rest of the class).","Judges tick the support checklist: hook, opinion, two supported reasons, counterargument, conclusion.","The council votes green or red.","Each checklist tick = 1 point; each green vote = 1 point."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is the purpose of an opinion text?","answer":"to persuade the reader","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"الإقناع.","options":["to persuade the reader","to tell a fairy tale","to give directions","to describe a picture"],"dok":1,"skill":"genre"},{"q":"What is a *counterargument*?","answer":"the opposite opinion that some people have","explanation":"Counterargument.","explanation_ar":"الرأي المخالف.","options":["the title of the text","a kind of fact","the first reason","the opposite opinion that some people have"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which belongs in Paragraph 1 of your opinion text?","answer":"a hook and your opinion","explanation":"Organization.","explanation_ar":"جملة جذب ورأي.","options":["a hook and your opinion","the counterargument only","the conclusion only","a list of rules"],"dok":1,"skill":"organization"},{"q":"Which linking word introduces your answer to the other side?","answer":"However,","explanation":"Answer.","explanation_ar":"However.","options":["However,","First,","For example,","Did you know"],"dok":1,"skill":"linking words"},{"q":"Which sentence about the school rule is correct?","answer":"Our school should stop selling sugary drinks.","explanation":"should + verb.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Our school should to stop selling sugary drinks.","Our school should stops selling sugary drinks.","Our school should stop selling sugary drinks.","Our school should stopping selling sugary drinks."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which is the BEST conclusion for an opinion about a calm corner?","answer":"For these reasons, a calm corner would help every student feel ready to learn.","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"أفضل خاتمة.","options":["Calm corners have cushions.","For these reasons, a calm corner would help every student feel ready to learn.","Did you know that cushions are soft?","Some people say corners are small."],"dok":2,"skill":"conclusions"},{"q":"Which tone is BEST for writing to the school council?","answer":"polite and confident","explanation":"Tone.","explanation_ar":"مهذبة وواثقة.","options":["rude and angry","silly and joking","polite and confident","sad and worried"],"dok":2,"skill":"tone"},{"q":"How long should your opinion text be?","answer":"120–150 words","explanation":"Length.","explanation_ar":"120–150 كلمة.","options":["20–30 words","120–150 words","500 words","one sentence"],"dok":1,"skill":"length"},{"q":"A partner says, *Your second reason has no support.* What should you add?","answer":"a fact, a number, an example or an expert source","explanation":"Revising.","explanation_ar":"دعم.","options":["another hook","a new title","more exclamation marks","a fact, a number, an example or an expert source"],"dok":3,"skill":"revising"},{"q":"Which reason + support for screen-free lunch is the MOST persuasive?","answer":"Playing with friends helps build friendships; for example, our class became closer after we started playing football at lunch.","explanation":"Supported reason.","explanation_ar":"الأكثر إقناعًا.","options":["Screens are nice, but I don't like them.","Phones are expensive.","Playing with friends helps build friendships; for example, our class became closer after we started playing football at lunch.","Lunch is at twelve o'clock."],"dok":3,"skill":"evaluate"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'rule': a sign with school rules"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'sugary': a can of soda with sugar cubes"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'acid': a tooth with a small hole"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'fiber': carrots, beans and whole bread"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'replace': a soda can swapped for a water bottle"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'counterargument': two speech bubbles facing each other"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'council': students sitting around a table voting"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-01","prompt":"Students presenting healthy-school rules to a class council."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-02","prompt":"Four healthy-school rule cards."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L05-U2-LS5-03","prompt":"A megaphone-shaped opinion planner."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V01","script":"rule. Our school has a new healthy rule."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V02","script":"sugary. Sugary drinks can damage teeth."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V03","script":"acid. Germs make acid that damages teeth."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V04","script":"fiber. Vegetables have lots of fiber."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V05","script":"replace. Replace soda with water."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V06","script":"counterargument. Answer the counterargument with a reason."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-V07","script":"council. The student council will vote on the rule."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-T1","script":"**Card A – No sugary drinks at school** · Fact: one can of soda can contain about eight teaspoons of sugar · Fact: dentists say sugar helps germs in the mouth make acid that damages teeth · Example: students feel tired soon after a sugary drink at break **Card B – Fruit or vegetables in every lunch box** · Fact: fruit and vegetables have vitamins and fiber · Expert: the World Health Organization recommends eating at least 400 grams of fruit and vegetables a day · Example: an apple or carrot sticks are easy to carry **Card C – Screen-free lunch breaks** · Fact: talking and playing with friends helps build friendships · Fact: looking at screens for a long time can tire your eyes · Example: students who play outside at lunch come back more active **Card D – A calm corner in every classroom** · Fact: slow, deep breathing can help the body feel calm · Fact: short rests can reduce stress before tests · Example: a quiet corner with cushions and books helps students relax for a few minutes"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L05-U2-LS5-VID","script":"The Healthy School Council is listening! Which new rule will you suggest? Read the rule cards: no sugary drinks, fruit in every lunch box, screen-free lunch, a calm corner. Did you know that one can of soda can contain about eight teaspoons of sugar?… Paragraph 1: hook + opinion. Paragraph 2: two supported reasons, the other side and a conclusion! Be polite, be confident and use facts. Now present to the council!"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Eating fruit, vegetables, grains and protein in the right amounts is a ___.","answer":"balanced diet","explanation":"Balanced diet.","explanation_ar":"نظام غذائي متوازن.","options":["routine","balanced diet","posture","council"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Hamza twisted his ankle during the match. His ___ needed rest and ice.","answer":"injury","explanation":"Injury.","explanation_ar":"إصابته.","options":["vitamin","habit","fitness","injury"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Sitting with a straight back and relaxed shoulders is good ___.","answer":"posture","explanation":"Posture.","explanation_ar":"وضعية.","options":["stress","energy","posture","acid"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"After two weeks of rest, she ___ from the flu and went back to school.","answer":"recovered","explanation":"Recover.","explanation_ar":"تعافت.","options":["hydrated","recovered","replaced","concentrated"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Drink water before, during and after sport to ___ your body.","answer":"hydrate","explanation":"Hydrate.","explanation_ar":"تروي.","options":["recover","maintain","relax","hydrate"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which health word is built from an adjective + *-ness*?","answer":"weakness","explanation":"weak = adjective.","explanation_ar":"weakness.","options":["treatment","movement","weakness","equipment"],"dok":1,"skill":"suffixes","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*The coach saw a big **improvement** in Hamza's running.* What is the base word and its part of speech?","answer":"improve – verb","explanation":"Take off -ment.","explanation_ar":"improve فعل.","options":["improve – verb","improvement – adjective","prove – noun","improving – adverb"],"dok":2,"skill":"suffixes","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*Doctors **recommend** at least 60 minutes of activity a day.* *Recommend* means ___.","answer":"advise as the best thing to do","explanation":"Recommend.","explanation_ar":"يوصون.","options":["advise as the best thing to do","forbid","forget","measure"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary in context","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Reason: *Breakfast helps students learn.* Which is the STRONGEST support?","answer":"Many studies suggest that students who eat breakfast concentrate better in the morning.","explanation":"Reliable support.","explanation_ar":"الأقوى.","options":["Breakfast is my favorite meal.","Many studies suggest that students who eat breakfast concentrate better in the morning.","Breakfast makes students 100 times smarter.","My sister likes eggs."],"dok":2,"skill":"supporting evidence","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which linking phrase BEST introduces an expert source?","answer":"According to doctors,","explanation":"Expert source.","explanation_ar":"According to.","options":["For example,","In my house,","According to doctors,","Once upon a time,"],"dok":1,"skill":"linking phrases","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which is the best HOOK for an opinion text about breakfast?","answer":"Did you know that your brain uses energy even when you are sitting still?","explanation":"Fact hook.","explanation_ar":"الأفضل.","options":["Breakfast is a meal.","This text is about breakfast.","I am going to write about breakfast now.","Did you know that your brain uses energy even when you are sitting still?"],"dok":1,"skill":"hooks","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which counterargument and answer fit an opinion that *schools should open a breakfast club*?","answer":"Some people say families should make breakfast at home. However, many parents leave for work very early.","explanation":"Counter + answer.","explanation_ar":"الأنسب.","options":["Some people like eggs. However, I like dates.","Some people say families should make breakfast at home. However, many parents leave for work very early.","Breakfast is early. However, lunch is late.","Some people say clubs are fun. However, fun is good."],"dok":3,"skill":"counterargument","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which conclusion repeats the opinion in NEW words?","answer":"For these reasons, a morning breakfast club would help every student start the day ready to learn.","explanation":"Conclusion.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة جيدة.","options":["For these reasons, a morning breakfast club would help every student start the day ready to learn.","Did you know that breakfast means breaking the fast?","Some people say breakfast is boring.","First, breakfast gives energy."],"dok":2,"skill":"conclusions","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which support for a breakfast opinion is WEAK?","answer":"Breakfast is good because it is good.","explanation":"Circular reason.","explanation_ar":"ضعيف.","options":["Protein helps the body grow.","Whole grains give long-lasting energy.","Hungry students find it hard to concentrate.","Breakfast is good because it is good."],"dok":2,"skill":"weak support","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"}],"unit_writing":{"task":"Should our school open a free 'Breakfast Club' before classes? Write a two-paragraph opinion text (120–150 words). Paragraph 1: a hook and your opinion. Paragraph 2: two reasons with support (facts, examples or experts from the article), a counterargument with your answer, and a conclusion.","model":"Did you know that after a night's sleep, your body has gone eight to ten hours without food? I believe our school should open a free Breakfast Club before classes. (new paragraph) First, breakfast gives our brains the energy they need. Many studies suggest that students who eat a healthy breakfast concentrate and remember better in the morning. Second, a club would help students who have no time at home. For example, some of my classmates leave home very early and come to school hungry. Some people say that breakfast is the family's job, not the school's. However, many parents start work early, and a school club would support them. For these reasons, I strongly believe a Breakfast Club would help every student start the day ready to learn.","marks":20}});
